window.LUNA_CHAPTERS=(window.LUNA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":226,"title":"Chapter 226 The Blanket","paragraphs":["\"Why are all my photos stored back here?\" Eira asked.","Gwen glanced up from the box. \"That photographer, Lainey, said she was making a documentary. She’s been asking about children who grew up here and went on to do something with their lives.\"","She gave Eira a small smile.","\"You’re the biggest success story we have. But you asked me to keep your information private, so I put everything away. I didn’t want her digging through your records or catching anything on camera.\"","A chill brushed the back of Eira’s neck.","It sounded as if Lainey had been asking about her.","Then again, a documentary covered people as well as places. Lainey’s questions were not suspicious on the surface.","\"What has she been doing since she arrived?\" Eira asked.","\"Mostly talking to people around the orphanage. She says she’s collecting stories for the film.\" Gwen frowned. \"To be honest, it feels less like a fundraising video and more like she’s looking for something.\"","\"What kind of something?\"","\"Nothing specific enough to make me stop her. If she had crossed a line, someone would’ve come to me.\"","Eira nodded, though the answer did little to ease her mind.","She turned back to the storage box and lifted a stack of old photographs. Beneath them, she found a small bundle sealed in a clear plastic bag.","Inside was a piece of blue-striped cotton.","Eira frowned. \"What is this?\"","Gwen went still.","\"That’s the blanket you were wrapped in when they found you.\"","Eira looked up. \"Mine?\"","Gwen nodded.","Every child brought to the orphanage had their clothes washed, labeled, and stored. Most of those items were ordinary. This one was not.","Eira opened the bag carefully.","The cotton was soft with age. Tiny airplanes had been stitched between the blue stripes.","\"That was expensive fabric back then,\" Gwen said quietly. \"High-end baby clothes. We thought your family might have lost you by accident instead of leaving you behind.\"","Eira ran her thumb over one of the faded airplanes.","\"We spent fifteen days checking with every neighboring Pack along the border,\" Gwen continued. \"We asked about missing pups, searched the shelters, and contacted the regional records office. Nothing came up.\"","She hesitated.","\"There was one strange detail. The blanket was made for a boy.\"","Eira’s head snapped up. \"A boy?\"","\"The pattern, the size, even the way it was sewn. Everything suggested it had been bought for a male pup.\"","Gwen lowered herself into the old office chair.","\"You know the rest. You grew up here, worked harder than anyone, and built a life far beyond this town. You never forgot the Omega House either. You’ve been giving back ever since you had the means.\"","Eira set the blanket down and wrapped her arms around Gwen.","\"Thank you,\" she whispered. \"For taking me in. For giving me a home.\"","Gwen patted her back.","\"All right. Don’t make me cry before breakfast.\"","Eira pulled away, smiling through the tightness in her throat.","Gwen’s expression softened. \"Do you want to look for your family?\"","Eira glanced at the storage box.","\"We kept the paper records. There isn’t much, but it’s a place to start.\"","Eira pressed her lips together.","\"If the answers are there, I’ll find them.\"","That was not quite an answer, and Gwen knew it.","\"If I was left on purpose, then there’s nothing to chase,\" Eira said. \"But if I was lost, my family may still be looking for me.\"","She folded the blanket back into the plastic bag.","\"I just need to give them a reason to find me.\"","Gwen reached for her hand. \"You don’t have to prove that you’re worth finding.\"","\"I know.\"","But knowing that and believing her family would find her were two different things.","People searched for what they remembered. If her family had lost a little boy, they might never think to look for the woman she had become.","Eira glanced toward the dining hall, where Lainey was still filming the children.","Lainey was the only person who had recently gone out of her way to learn about Eira’s past.","--","In Palo Alto, Alpha Killian took a screenshot of the address Eira had sent him and forwarded it to Lila without saying a word.","A voice message came back almost at once.","\"You’re so immature.\"","\"You’re the immature one!\"","Alpha Killian ignored the rest of her rant.","His flight landed a short time later. Natalie had arranged a driver, but Alpha Killian waved him off and took the wheel himself.","While he drove, he sent Eira his itinerary. She was already reviewing the information Gwen had given her about Sam, including possible routes, places to stay, and transportation options.","Eira could handle rough conditions. She had traveled alone before and knew how to take care of herself.","She was only worried about Alpha Killian.","After sending Alpha Killian the details, Eira questioned the longtime staff.","The gatekeeper, kitchen staff, and dorm supervisors gave her the same answer. Lainey had asked about the orphanage’s history and whether any former residents had gone on to become successful or appeared in the news.","Most had told her little. One of the nursery workers pulled Eira aside.","\"I mentioned you,\" she admitted. \"Miss Gwen showed me an article about your work and asked me to read it to the kids. One of them recognized you as Big Sister Eira, so I told Lainey you grew up here and now work in Palo Alto.\"","\"When?\"","\"Three days ago.\"","\"Did she ask anything else?\"","\"Not really. She thanked me and went back to playing with the children. They adore her.\"","That answer should have reassured Eira. Instead, it left her with more questions.","Eira thanked the woman and stepped back into the hallway.","\"Oh, and she was asking about the old records earlier,\" the woman added. \"I saw her heading toward the archive room.\"","Eira stopped. \"The records room?\"","\"She said she wanted some background for the documentary. I didn’t think much of it.\"","Eira thanked her and headed down the hall.","The archive door stood partly open. Inside, Lainey was filming the faded photographs and rows of filing cabinets. When she heard Eira approach, she lowered the camera and turned with a pleasant smile.","\"Eira. I was just looking for you.\"","\"Were you?\"","Lainey’s smile stayed in place, but her grip tightened around the camera.","\"I wanted footage of the older part of the building. It has character.\"","\"The records room?\"","\"I was curious.\"","\"Can I see what you filmed?\"","Lainey studied her for a moment, then handed over the camera.","\"Sure.\"","Eira skimmed the footage. It showed the grounds, the children, and a few old photographs. Nothing private or obviously invasive.","She returned the camera.","\"You’ve asked a lot about the orphanage’s history,\" Eira said. \"You also wanted to know whether any former residents became successful.\"","Lainey blinked once, then recovered.","\"History gives the documentary a stronger story. A successful former resident gives people someone to connect with. It’s good publicity.\"","\"Someone told you about me.\"","Lainey gave a small nod. \"Someone did.\"","\"If you plan to use my name or image, get permission first. The last outlet that interviewed me was a national news organization. My work involves federal security clearance, so people take the handling of my information seriously.\"","Lainey’s smile froze before smoothly returning.","\"Thanks for the warning. I wouldn’t dream of crossing a line.\"","\"Good luck with the shoot.\"","Eira turned and walked away.","The moment she disappeared around the corner, Lainey’s smile vanished. She had come to this remote stretch of Pack territory looking for something useful. Most of the staff had kept quiet, but she had finally learned that Eira had grown up there.","Then Eira had shown up and shut down the conversation.","Wasn’t she supposed to be busy dealing with Serena and the lawsuit?","Lainey pulled out her phone and called Serena.","She needed to know what had changed."]},{"number":227,"title":"Chapter 227 The Substitute","paragraphs":["Lainey slipped into a quiet corner of the courtyard and called Serena.","After a few polite words, she lowered her voice.","\"I’m out in the border territory filming. Guess who showed up?\"","Serena went quiet.","\"Eira,\" Lainey said. \"She’s back at the Omega House, nowhere near Palo Alto. That means she can’t keep an eye on you and Sebastian. You two get a little more breathing room.\"","Lainey had a talent for making every suggestion sound like a favor. She never pushed outright. She simply offered a tempting detail, then waited for someone to reach for it.","Serena took the bait.","\"Eira went back to the Omega House?\"","So that was why Alpha Sebastian had said Eira probably would not move forward with the lawsuit anytime soon.","\"Is something wrong?\" Lainey asked, her voice full of concern.","\"Something came up,\" Serena said. \"She was pressuring us hard, then suddenly backed off. She must have something more important to deal with.\"","\"Well, at least she’s off your back for now. As long as you’re okay.\"","\"Thanks, Lainey.\"","\"Of course.\" Lainey let a few seconds pass before adding, \"Still, what could be so important that she’d fly all the way out to the border?\"","Serena hesitated. \"I don’t know.\"","Lainey’s fingers tightened around her phone.","Was Eira looking for her birth family? Had someone finally uncovered a lead?","Her pulse quickened. The elevation was already making her chest feel tight.","Lainey’s body had never handled the mountain air well.She forced herself to breathe slowly.","\"Sorry,\" she said. \"I’m losing signal out here. I need to go.\"","Before Serena could ask another question, Lainey ended the call.","--","Meanwhile, Eira waited near the main entrance of the Omega House for Alpha Killian.","Her phone rang. Lila was calling.","\"Is my brother there yet?\"","\"Not yet.\" Eira glanced toward the gate. Cars passed along the highway, but none turned into the driveway.","\"So what did you bribe him with?\"","\"Eight hundred a day.\"","Lila went quiet for a second.","Then Eira heard her choke on her drink.","\"Hold on. Sorry.\" Lila coughed, then started laughing. \"Eight hundred? That’s not even a serious consulting fee for a man like my brother.\"","\"It was his number.\"","\"Please. Killian doesn’t need eight hundred dollars. He probably spends more than that on coffee.\"","Eira glanced toward the empty driveway. \"Are you done?\"","\"Not even close. With his face and that body, he could charge a fortune for a private appearance.\"","\"Lila.\"","\"What? I’m being supportive.\"","\"You’re being ridiculous.\"","\"I’m being honest. If he walked into one of those celebrity charity events, someone would pay ten grand just to have him stand next to their table.\"","Eira had no idea how to respond to that.","A car horn sounded near the gate.","She turned as a black Rolls-Royce Cullinan rolled onto the property.","Alpha Killian stepped out, tall and composed in a dark wool coat. The guard straightened before waving him through.","\"I have to go,\" Eira said.","\"What? Why?\"","\"The escort is here.\"","Lila burst out laughing.","Eira ended the call before Lila could say anything worse and hurried toward the car.","\"He’s with me,\" she told the guard.","Alpha Killian closed the driver’s door and walked toward her. The wind caught Eira’s hair and blew it across her face. She pushed it behind her ears, but the cold had already turned the tip of her nose pink.","Alpha Killian frowned and stepped in front of her, blocking the wind with his body.","\"You should have worn a hat.\"","\"I forgot.\"","\"You forgot a hat in the middle of winter?\"","\"I had other things to worry about.\" She looked toward the main building. \"Come on. Gwen wants me to bring someone I trust before I follow Sam’s lead.\"","\"Then let’s go.\"","\"You’re not tired?\"","\"No.\"","They started toward the building.","Eira lowered her voice. \"Lainey is here.\"","Alpha Killian’s expression cooled.","\"Then watch what you say.\"","\"Because of our cover?\"","\"The married-couple story.\"","Eira glanced up at him. \"Does the package include a warranty?\"","Alpha Killian looked down at her.","She had no idea where she had picked up that phrase, and he decided not to ask.","\"Yes,\" he said. \"It does.\"","For eight hundred dollars a day, Eira thought, that seemed fair.","Alpha Killian had wanted to inspect the property before they left. The Omega House sat near the edge of Pack territory, where city services were limited and patrol routes mattered. He wanted to see the security system, the fence line, and how the border Pack protected the children.","Eira was already pulling him toward Gwen’s office.","He knew Gwen’s background. She was fifty-one, had received a regional service award, and had run the Omega House for most of Eira’s life.","She was not just the director.","She was Eira’s family.","Eira knocked once and opened the door.","\"Miss Gwen, he’s here.\" She stepped aside. \"This is Killian Sterling.\"","Gwen stood and reached for her reading glasses.","\"Mr. Sterling.\"","\"Killian is fine.\" He shook her hand. \"Eira calls me that.\"","Gwen studied him for a moment. He was young, powerful, and clearly accustomed to being obeyed. Still, he had come all the way out here because Eira had asked.","That counted for something.","\"You’re prepared to protect her?\"","Alpha Killian took a business card from his wallet and set it on the desk.","\"If anything happens, call that number. If Eira is hurt because of me, the Sterling family will take responsibility.\"","His voice was quiet, but there was nothing casual about the promise.","Gwen picked up the card and looked at him more carefully.","\"Thank you,\" she said.","Alpha Killian nodded.","Gwen had seen men promise to take care of Eira before. Most of them had offered words and nothing else. Alpha Killian had come with a plan, transportation, and a way to reach him directly.","She walked them outside.","\"The county is rougher than Palo Alto,\" she warned Eira. \"Stay together, keep your phones charged, and call me if anything feels wrong.\"","\"I will.\"","They were almost at the gate when Lainey stepped out of the dining hall with her camera hanging from one shoulder.","\"Killian,\" Lainey called, bright and friendly. \"What brings you all the way out here?\"","He kept walking.","\"Not your concern.\"","Her smile tightened, but she turned to Eira instead.","\"You two seem pretty close.\"","\"Glad you can tell,\" Alpha Killian said without looking back.","A flicker of annoyance crossed Lainey’s face.","\"So where are you headed now?\"","\"Back to Palo Alto,\" Eira said.","\"Already? You just got here.\"","Before the question could turn into an interrogation, Gwen stepped in.","\"That was my doing,\" she said easily. \"I asked Eira to come back because something urgent came up. It’s taken care of now, so she needs to get going.\"","Lainey’s eyes moved from Gwen to Eira, then settled on Alpha Killian.","Urgent.","So Alpha Killian was covering for Eira. And now Gwen was covering for her too.","Lainey gave a small nod, as if she accepted the explanation.","\"Of course,\" she said. \"I hope everything worked out.\"","\"Thanks,\" Eira replied.","Lainey’s smile stayed polite, but her mind was already working.","Whatever had brought Eira here, it was more important than Lainey had expected."]},{"number":228,"title":"Chapter 228 The Search Begins","paragraphs":["The moment the SUV pulled away from the Omega House, Eira opened her tablet and pulled up the plan she had prepared earlier.","\"It’s four forty,\" she said. \"We’ll reach the county line around five thirty. We’ll grab dinner first, then check the neighborhood where Sam’s uncle used to live. Between seven and eight, people should be home and willing to talk.\"","Alpha Killian kept one hand on the wheel. His other rested near the gearshift, relaxed but ready. He glanced at her tablet, then at the focused crease between her brows.","\"After that, we can check the three high schools in the county. They all sit along the same main road, so we can cover them quickly. If we don’t find anything tonight, we start again in the morning. Then we get a hotel.\"","Eira finally looked up. \"Does that work for you?\"","\"You’re in charge.\"","\"That sounds suspiciously like you’re trying to avoid responsibility.\"","\"I’m the hired help.\" His mouth twitched. \"Eight hundred dollars a day. I follow orders.\"","The number reminded her of Lila’s ridiculous comments about Alpha Killian’s private appearance fee.","\"Killian.\"","\"Yes?\"","\"Eight hundred is not enough.\"","His silver-gray eyes slid toward her. \"Then name your price.\"","Eira hesitated. \"A thousand?\"","\"Fine.\"","He said it so easily that she narrowed her eyes. \"You didn’t even negotiate.\"","\"You were worried about underpaying me.\"","\"I was being fair.\"","\"I know.\"","The warmth in his voice made her look back at the tablet.","They reached the diner five minutes ahead of schedule. The small roadside place was bright and crowded, its windows fogged from the cold. The smell of coffee, fried onions, and warm pie filled the air.","When Alpha Killian walked in wearing a tailored coat, several heads turned. A woman at the counter whispered something to her friend, who glanced over and nearly spilled her coffee.","Eira led him to a corner booth before anyone could come over.","They ordered grilled chicken, soup, fries, and coffee. Eira chose the cheapest items on the menu, but Alpha Killian noticed.","\"Don’t worry about the bill,\" he said quietly.","\"I’m not.\"","\"You are.\"","She looked up from her menu.","\"We’re here to find Sam,\" Alpha Killian continued. \"Eat something warm. Get a decent room. Stop apologizing for taking care of yourself.\"","The words settled somewhere deep in her chest.","She closed the menu. \"Fine. But I’m still paying your fee.\"","\"I’ll send an invoice.\"","\"You’d better.\"","After dinner, they drove to the neighborhood where Sam’s uncle had lived.","The street sat beyond the county’s better-maintained roads. Puddles filled the cracked pavement, old trash cans leaned beside narrow porches, and damp smoke drifted from backyard fire pits.","A few children in puffy winter coats raced between the buildings while their parents called after them.","They had barely reached the first row of apartments when people began watching them.","A man sitting on a porch glanced at the photo on Eira’s phone and muttered, \"Wonder if they’re here about Nate.\"","Eira caught the name and approached a group of older women gathered beneath an awning.","\"Evening. Sorry to bother you. Did a man named Jordan come around here recently?\"","She showed them the photo.","One woman nodded. \"I’ve seen him. He came looking for Nate. After that, Nate told everyone the family was getting a fresh start somewhere up north.\"","\"Did he say where?\"","\"No,\" another woman said. \"He kept that part to himself.\"","\"Are you family?\" someone asked.","\"I’m Sam’s sister.\"","The women’s expressions softened.","\"You’re the girl from the Omega House,\" one of them said. \"Sam’s sister. Sweet boy.\"","\"Nate called him the family’s good-luck charm,\" another added. \"Said Sam would bring them better luck wherever they went.\"","\"Good-luck charm, my ass.\" A third woman snorted. \"That boy hauled trash, watched the little kids, and got slapped whenever they cried. Nate treated him like free labor.\"","Eira’s jaw tightened.","Then one woman lowered her voice. \"Nate used to brag about getting SSI for Sam. Said the boy brought in a few hundred dollars a month.\"","\"SSI for what?\" someone asked.","\"Autism, I think. And Nate claimed Sam was missing a thumb too.\"","Eira went still.","\"What?\"","Sam had left the Omega House with both hands intact. Eira had helped him dress. She knew exactly what she had seen.","Eira drew in a slow breath, then looked back at the women.","\"Did Nate mention where they were taking Sam?\"","The women exchanged glances.","\"Some kind of school,\" one said. \"A place for kids who need extra help.\"","\"A special school?\" another asked. \"There isn’t one in this county.\"","\"That’s still helpful,\" Eira said.","She pulled a business card from her wallet and handed it to the oldest woman.","\"If you remember anything else, please call me. Any time.\"","The woman studied the card. \"You really looking for that boy?\"","\"He’s my brother.\"","The woman’s expression softened. \"Then I hope you find him.\"","Eira thanked them and led Alpha Killian back toward the SUV.","Alpha Killian glanced at her. \"What do we know?\"","He couldn’t make out every word through the women’s overlapping voices and rapid-fire local expressions. But he saw Eira’s face change, and that told him enough.","\"Beta Jordan came looking for Nate. Nate moved the family north, claimed Sam was receiving SSI, and told people the boy was missing a thumb.\"","Alpha Killian’s jaw tightened.","\"Which isn’t true,\" Eira said. \"Sam left the Omega House with both hands intact.\"","She searched the nearby school districts on her phone.","\"The woman may have meant a special education program, not a separate school. There’s a nonpublic school in the next county, but we need to verify it.\"","\"Can we go tonight?\"","\"The schools are closed. And they can’t release Sam’s records without legal authorization.\"","\"Then I’ll make the calls.\"","While Eira checked district websites, Alpha Killian contacted his attorney. A few minutes later, Miles sent an update.","Miles: The county registrar can meet with you at eight tomorrow morning. They’ll verify whether Sam’s name appears in recent transfers, but they can’t release protected records without authorization.","Eira glanced at Alpha Killian. \"That was fast.\"","\"Money buys speed. Not access.\"","She almost smiled. \"You sound responsible.\"","\"I have my moments.\"","Eira opened the website for the specialized school. Its polished pages were full of bright photos and vague testimonials. There were no parent complaints, angry reviews, or local discussions.","That did not prove anything. Small private schools often had little online presence.","Still, the site looked too clean.","\"It’s our best lead,\" she said.","\"We’ll check it in the morning.\"","They returned to the SUV. Eira climbed into the passenger seat and kept scrolling through the school’s website.","\"Give me a minute,\" Alpha Killian said.","Before she could ask where he was going, he crossed the road to a taco truck closing beneath a string of yellow lights.","He returned with two paper bags and two cups of hot chocolate.","\"Chicken tacos,\" he said, handing her one bag. \"And churros.\"","Eira wrapped her hands around the warm cup. \"You got both?\"","\"Something spicy and something sweet.\"","The smell of grilled meat, lime, and cinnamon drifted through the cold air.","\"You went through all that trouble for tacos?\"","\"You were hungry.\"","\"I never said I was.\"","\"You didn’t have to.\"","Their fingers brushed as she took the bags.","\"Thank you.\"","After the tacos, they found a decent hotel near the highway.","The place was small but clean, with warm lighting, dark wood floors, and a front desk decorated with winter wreaths. Alpha Killian handed over his ID. Eira placed hers beside it.","\"The reservation is under my name,\" she told the clerk.","The clerk checked the screen. \"Two deluxe king rooms. Next door to each other?\"","\"That works.\"","A few minutes later, they reached the second floor.","Alpha Killian stopped outside his door. \"Get some sleep. Tomorrow is the important day.\"","\"I will.\"","She entered her room and closed the door.","A few seconds later, his door clicked shut next to hers."]},{"number":229,"title":"Chapter 229 The Boy in the Ambulance","paragraphs":["Morning came gray and bitterly cold.","After washing up, Eira knocked on Alpha Killian ’s door. He opened it almost immediately. Faint shadows sat beneath his silver-gray eyes.","The hotel mattress had been too soft, the walls too thin, and freight trucks had rumbled along the highway most of the night. Alpha Killian looked as composed as ever.","\"Breakfast here or on the road?\" he asked.","\"On the road.\"","They met the county education liaison in the lobby. He was waiting beside a county-issued sedan with a folder tucked beneath one arm.","\"The registrar is ready for you,\" he said. \"We’ll start there. If the district finds a possible match, I’ll contact the school and arrange a meeting.\"","Eira stopped at the café near the front desk and bought three breakfast bags: sausage, egg, and cheese biscuits, hash browns, coffee, and bottled orange juice.","She could eat while they drove. Alpha Killian needed both hands on the wheel, and he had barely slept. She made a mental note to get her license as soon as possible.","Forty minutes later, they pulled into the county education office.","The registrar checked Eira’s identification and reviewed the documents Gwen had provided to confirm her connection to Sam.","\"I need to be clear about what I can and can’t do,\" she said. \"I can’t show you protected student records. But I can search recent transfers using Sam’s legal name, age, and date of birth. If I find a possible match, I can contact the receiving school and ask them to verify the student’s safety.\"","\"And if his name was changed?\" Eira asked.","\"Then the search may come back empty. If this involves an endangered child, law enforcement or a court order can request more information.\"","Eira tightened her hand around her phone.","The registrar made several calls. She asked about recent transfers, private placements, and residential programs in the neighboring district. Ten minutes later, she put down the phone.","\"There’s a private residential program in the neighboring district that recently admitted a boy who matches Sam’s age and support needs. The student is registered under a different name. It’s only a possible match, but it’s the closest lead I found.\"","Eira’s breath caught. \"Can you tell me what name they used?\"","\"I’m sorry. Not without proper authorization.\" The registrar glanced at the liaison. \"But I can ask the school administrator to meet with you. The county office can verify the inquiry without releasing the student’s file.\"","It was not enough, but it was a lead.","They left the office and climbed into their vehicles. The liaison’s sedan pulled onto the highway, and Alpha Killian followed.","Half an hour into the drive, Eira opened one of the breakfast bags.","\"You need to eat.\"","\"I’m fine.\"","\"You look exhausted.\"","\"I’m driving.\"","\"That’s not an answer.\"","She unwrapped a sausage biscuit and held it out. Alpha Killian kept his eyes on the road, but after a moment, he leaned over and took it from her fingers.","Her fingertip brushed his lower lip.","His skin felt dry from the cold.","Eira quickly steadied the biscuit before it fell apart. \"I wiped my hands. It’s clean. You’ll survive one breakfast sandwich.\"","Alpha Killian gave her a sideways glance.","\"If you hate it, I’ll make you something better when we get home.\"","He finished the biscuit in two bites. Eira lifted the straw from the orange juice and held it out. He took a drink without complaint, then returned his attention to the road.","\"Make me breakfast sandwiches bigger than your fist,\" he said.","Eira blinked.","Then she remembered the homemade dishes she used to bring to Sterling Group. Everyone on the executive floor had received some except Alpha Killian .He had not forgotten.","A small smile tugged at her lips. \"You’re still holding a grudge?\"","\"I remember what matters.\"","The warmth in his voice eased something tight in her chest.","The county sedan eventually turned off the highway onto a private road. A sign marked the entrance to a residential program for students with intensive support needs.","A security guard stepped out of the gatehouse. The liaison lowered his window, showed his county identification, and explained the registrar’s request.","The guard made a quick call, then opened the gate.","Inside, the campus was quiet and carefully maintained. A landscaped pond divided the main drive. The academic buildings stood to the right, while the residential wing sat behind a line of tall cedar trees on the left.","The vehicles turned toward the academic buildings.","They had gone less than a hundred yards when an ambulance siren cut through the morning.","Eira looked in the side mirror.","An ambulance came from the residential wing with its lights flashing. It sped past the gatehouse and disappeared onto the highway.","She could not see who was inside.","The road curved, blocking her view, but a cold weight had already settled in her chest.","The liaison parked near the main entrance and led them inside.","The building was clean and well maintained, but the halls were loud. Voices echoed behind closed doors. A student shouted from one classroom while a staff member repeated the same calm instruction.","\"Residential programs can be intense,\" the liaison said carefully. \"The students have different support needs. Some are quiet. Some need constant supervision. A few may become aggressive when they’re overwhelmed.\"","Alpha Killian turned his head and gave him a hard look.","The liaison stopped talking.","They reached the administration office. Before he could knock, a man in a staff polo opened the door. He recognized the county liaison and forced a polite smile.","\"Good morning.\"","\"This is Mr. Sterling, and this is Ms. Crawford,\" the liaison said. \"The registrar asked us to follow up on a possible transfer.\"","The staff member’s smile faded when he saw Eira’s phone.","She held up Sam’s photograph.","\"This is my brother. His name is Sam.\"","The color drained from the man’s face.","Alpha Killian ’s voice turned cold. \"Where is he?\"","\"Everything is under control,\" the staff member said too quickly.","A principal stepped out from behind a desk. He looked calmer than the others, but sweat darkened the collar of his shirt.","\"The student is registered here as Jae,\" he said. \"J-A-E.\"","Eira’s brow tightened.","The principal glanced at the staff member.","\"Jae is autistic,\" the man said. \"He is mostly nonverbal and needs close supervision. He likes to climb. Trees, stairwells, fences. We have staff assigned to monitor him.\"","\"Then how did he get out of a second-floor window?\" Alpha Killian asked.","The man swallowed.","\"We found him outside the residential wing early this morning. He had fallen from a window. We called emergency services right away.\"","\"Why are you saying it like you’re not sure?\" Eira asked.","\"We are sure,\" the principal cut in. \"The fall was from the second floor. The ambulance crew took him to County General.\"","Eira’s stomach dropped.","The ambulance at the gate. The flashing lights. The residential wing.","Sam had been inside it.","Her hands turned cold. \"When did this happen?\"","\"Just after dawn.\"","\"And you waited until now to tell anyone?\"","No one argued.","Eira was already running toward the SUV.","They reached County General less than twenty minutes later.","Alpha Killian stopped at the emergency entrance, and Eira jumped out before the vehicle had fully settled.","She hurried to the reception desk.","\"A fifteen-year-old boy was brought in from a residential school this morning,\" she said. \"He’s listed under the name Jae.\"","\"Are you listed as family or an emergency contact?\"","\"I’m his sister. Here’s my ID.\"","The nurse checked the computer again.","\"The school listed an old emergency contact. We’ve been trying to reach them for hours, but no one has answered.\"","Then she read it aloud.","Eira froze.","She knew that number.","It belonged to Alpha Sebastian."]},{"number":230,"title":"Chapter 230 The Boy Behind the Glass","paragraphs":["Eira did not wait for the elevator. She took the stairs two at a time, her boots striking the concrete until she reached the surgical floor.","She knew she could not get past the double doors marked SURGERY.","AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL ONLY.","Still, she kept walking until a nurse stopped her near the waiting area.","\"Ma’am, you need to stay behind the line.\"","\"I’m his sister.\"","\"I understand, but the surgical unit is restricted. Please wait here.\"","Eira stopped just outside the doors.","A few minutes later, Alpha Killian came around the corner. He had stayed at the emergency desk to get an update and make sure the hospital had the correct contact information.","No one could tell him much. Sam was in surgery, and the doctors would speak with the family when they had something definite to report.","Alpha Killian found Eira standing perfectly still among the other waiting families. She was not pacing or twisting her hands. She looked frozen.","Then he saw the tears running down her cheeks.","\"Eira.\" His voice was low. \"The nurse said the injury is to his leg. They found no obvious head trauma.\"","\"Killian.\" Her whisper broke. \"If I had come last night...\"","\"Don’t.\" He stepped in front of her. \"Even if you had come, the school would not have let you through that gate. You couldn’t have known what was happening inside.\"","\"This is Sebastian’s fault.\" Her voice shook. \"He buried that boy in a place like this, then couldn’t even be bothered to check on him.\"","Alpha Killian did not argue.","Eira wiped at her cheeks, but more tears followed.","He brushed one away with his thumb. Her skin was cold. Without a word, he took off his coat and draped it around her shoulders. The wool still held his warmth.","\"Listen to me.\" His voice stayed calm and firm. \"We wait for the surgeon. If this hospital can’t provide what Sam needs, we arrange a transfer. A trauma center, a children’s hospital, wherever the doctors recommend. Money and planes are not the problem.\"","The certainty in his voice finally broke through her fear.","\"Killian, I’m scared.\" She gripped the front of his shirt. \"I’m scared Sam won’t make it. I took Sebastian back to the orphanage. I gave Sam his number.\"","Alpha Killian’s jaw tightened.","\"You brought Sebastian back because you believed he was family. You gave Sam a way to contact him because you cared what happened to that boy.\" He lowered himself in front of her and rested his hands lightly on her knees. \"Sebastian abused that trust. He took Sam and abandoned him. That is on Sebastian. Not you.\"","Eira shook her head, crying silently.","\"This has nothing to do with who you love or who you try to help,\" Alpha Killian continued. \"It has to do with what Sebastian chose to do. Do you understand?\"","\"I hear you.\"","\"That’s not what I asked.\"","She looked down at him.","\"Do you understand that this is not your fault?\"","Eira pressed her lips together, then nodded.","Alpha Killian rose and wiped the last tear from her cheek.","Before he could say anything else, the hospital elevator opened.","The school’s principal arrived with the county liaison and two staff members. They approached in a rush, speaking over one another.","\"It was a tragic accident.\"","\"We’re prepared to discuss medical expenses.\"","\"The school has always followed safety procedures.\"","\"Please,\" Alpha Killian said.","His voice was quiet, but it cut through the hallway.","Everyone fell silent.","He turned toward the principal.","\"Not one more word about compensation or an accident until the surgeon tells us whether that boy will live.\"","The principal’s face went pale.","Alpha Killian stepped closer.","\"After that, you will provide every incident report, staffing record, camera log, and emergency call connected to Sam’s fall.\"","\"We cannot release confidential—\"","\"You can preserve them,\" Alpha Killian cut in. \"The county liaison is standing right there. If anything disappears before the investigation begins, your school will have a much bigger problem than a lawsuit.\"","The liaison’s expression hardened. \"He’s right. Do not alter or destroy anything.\"","The principal swallowed.","Behind the surgical doors, a red status light remained on.","Eira stared at it, wrapped in Alpha Killian’s coat, while the hallway fell silent around them.","Alpha Killian took out his phone and called Kate.","\"Book the first available flight to the county,\" he said. \"Bring Dr. Wood. Have our legal team contact the hospital and child protective services. No one discusses a settlement until the investigation is complete.\"","He ended the call, then returned with a cup of hot chocolate and placed it in Eira’s hands.","She wrapped her fingers around the warm cup. \"Thank you.\"","Before Alpha Killian could answer, the red light above the operating room went out.","A surgeon stepped through the doors and lowered his mask.","Eira rose so quickly that the chair scraped across the floor.","\"Doctor?\"","\"Are you Sam’s family?\"","\"I’m his sister.\"","The surgeon gave a brief nod. \"The surgery went well. Sam had a serious fracture in his leg, but the more urgent problem was bleeding inside his skull. We relieved the pressure and stabilized it. He’ll be moved to the ICU for close monitoring.\"","Eira’s knees weakened. She caught the back of the chair.","\"Is he out of danger?\" Alpha Killian asked.","\"He’s stable for now,\" the surgeon said. \"The next twenty-four hours will be important.\"","Eira swallowed. \"You said there were other injuries.\"","The surgeon’s expression turned grave.","\"During the examination, we found extensive bruising across his body. Some of it appears recent. Some injuries may be older. We also found marks that are concerning for possible human bites, along with signs of fractures that may not have received proper medical treatment.\"","Eira went cold.","\"Bites?\" Alpha Killian asked.","\"Marks consistent with possible bites,\" the surgeon clarified. \"We’ve documented everything and notified the hospital social worker. Because Sam is a minor and came from a residential program, the hospital is required to make a report to County Child Welfare. Law enforcement may also become involved.\"","\"He lives at the school,\" Alpha Killian said.","The surgeon held his gaze. \"Then the school will need to explain how those injuries happened. For now, the ICU team needs to keep him stable.\"","\"They will,\" Alpha Killian said.","A nurse led them to the ICU.","Sam lay beneath a thin blanket, his face pale against the white pillow. His injured leg was secured in a brace, and wires connected him to the monitors beside the bed. Bruises showed above the collar of his hospital gown.","Eira sat beside him, afraid to touch him. She watched the green line on the monitor rise and fall.","Alpha Killian stepped into the hall and made several calls.","When he returned, a nurse was standing beside the bed.","\"Sam will remain in the ICU until the doctors are satisfied that he’s stable,\" she said. \"After that, they’ll decide whether he can be moved to a private room.\"","Alpha Killian nodded. \"Understood.\"","Eira kept her eyes on Sam.","\"The surgeon documented the injuries,\" Alpha Killian said quietly. \"The hospital social worker has started the required reports.\"","\"The police,\" Eira whispered. \"I want them here.\"","\"They’ll be notified through the hospital’s report,\" Alpha Killian said. \"I’ll also make sure our attorney contacts the county investigators.\"","Eira finally looked at him. Her eyes were red, but her voice was steady.","\"I want to know who did this to him.\"","Alpha Killian’s expression hardened.","\"Then we’ll find out. We’ll do it properly, and whoever hurt Sam will answer for it.\""]},{"number":231,"title":"Chapter 231 The Boy Who Flinched","paragraphs":["Sam finally stirred near dusk.","Eira rose at once and leaned over the bed. \"Sam? Hey, sweetheart. You’re awake.\"","An oxygen tube rested beneath his nose. He blinked up at her, dazed and frightened, as if he could not believe she was real.","Maybe her call had reached him last night. Maybe he had heard her voice before he passed out.","Alpha Killian reached toward the call button.","Sam’s eyes flew wide.","The monitor jumped into a rapid, uneven beep. His whole body tensed beneath the blanket.","Eira caught Alpha Killian’s wrist before he could touch the button and pulled his hand out of Sam’s sight.","\"Hey, it’s okay.\" She bent closer. \"You’re safe. No one is going to hurt you.\"","She released Alpha Killian and pressed the button herself.","A nurse arrived with the doctor a moment later. The instant Sam saw the white coat, panic took over again. His breathing quickened, and his hands began to shake.","Eira stepped between him and the doctor.","\"Give him some space.\"","The doctor stopped.","\"It’s okay, honey,\" Eira whispered. \"You don’t have to be scared. He’s just here to check on you.\"","Alpha Killian watched Sam’s reaction, then looked at the doctor.","\"Lose the coat,\" he said quietly. \"Come back without it.\"","The doctor stepped into the hall and returned a moment later in blue hospital scrubs. Eira kept hold of Sam’s hand while the nurse checked his vitals and the doctor completed a brief exam.","Sam stayed tense, but he no longer panicked.","\"Keep talking to him,\" the doctor told Eira. \"Your voice seems to calm him.\"","Alpha Killian nodded toward the hallway. \"Stay with him.\"","He followed the doctor outside.","Eira settled back into the chair and looked down at the hand she was holding.","Then she saw it.","Sam’s right thumb was missing from the first joint.","Her breath caught.","The surgeon’s words came back to her. The bruises. The old fractures. The possible bite marks. Sam’s terror when Alpha Killian reached for the call button. The way he had reacted to the doctor’s coat.","What had happened to him over the past two years?","What had the school done to him during the days he had been there?","Eira forced the questions down. Sam was awake, injured, and still afraid. She would not make him relive anything before he was ready.","Tears blurred her vision.","Then Sam’s fingers tightened around hers.","\"Sis,\" he whispered.","The word came out rough and dry.","Eira wiped her eyes and smiled. \"Yeah. I’m right here.\"","\"Sis.\"","Two years ago, the first time Sam had called her that, something inside her had changed. He had become her little brother in every way that mattered.","Now he gave her a weak, crooked smile. It was dazed and trusting, almost boyish.","Her chest ached.","Sam had not been the child she spent the most time with at Miss Gwen’s home. He was simply the one she had grown soft for, the one she had secretly given her number to.","But it would not have mattered which child had reached for her. Any child looking at her with that much fear and trust would have broken her heart.","She had a hundred questions.","Who hurt him? Why had he been sent away? Why had someone cut off his thumb? What had happened at the school?","But Sam was exhausted, medicated, and barely able to speak.","Eira squeezed his hand.","\"Rest now,\" she whispered. \"We’ll talk later.\"","She would wait until the police arrived.","--","Hale Tower was finally quiet.","Alpha Sebastian had just finished the launch ceremony for the Snowmark account. At least that deal was secure. The problems waiting behind it had not gone anywhere.","His annual report was due next. The Carter Group’s shareholder meeting was only days away, and despite securing the Snowmark contract, Alpha Sebastian had still lost the Sovereign Processor Initiative.","Alpha Sebastian could already picture the older board members sitting around the conference table, smiling politely as they picked apart his performance.","His report was thin. He had no major project to announce and no breakthrough to show for the year.","Alpha Carter would find a way to make it worse. Fiona always did.","Alpha Sebastian pressed two fingers to the bridge of his nose.","A knock sounded at the door.","\"Come in.\"","Beta Jordan stepped inside with a tablet in hand. \"Alpha, your phone has been off all day. Fiona’s office forwarded her call to me.\"","Alpha Sebastian glanced at the dead phone on his desk. Then he remembered the unknown number that had called again and again during the night.","\"I forgot to turn it back on.\" He picked up the phone. \"Isn’t Fiona at headquarters? What does she want?\"","\"The Omega Home and the other orphanages are being included in one combined donation drive this year. No special exceptions. The internal memo went out this morning.\"","Beta Jordan hesitated.","\"There’s more.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked up.","\"The trip lead has been reassigned. Finn is handling it this year. Alpha Carter said you don’t need to spend your time on that kind of work anymore.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression darkened.","Beta Jordan did not need to spell it out. The Omega Home was where Eira had grown up. The Carter siblings knew exactly what they were doing.","The memo had already been distributed. Arguing now would only make him look defensive.","\"Understood.\"","Sebastian turned on his phone.","Notifications flooded the screen, but no new calls came through. He opened the call history.","The same unknown number appeared again and again.","More than twenty missed calls.","He tapped the number.","The area code was 530, somewhere in Northern California.","Sebastian froze.","That was where Sam had been moved.","Sam.","It had to be him.","He hit redial."]},{"number":232,"title":"Chapter 232 The Phone Full of Missed Calls","paragraphs":["The line went dead.","Alpha Sebastian stared at the unfamiliar number on his screen. His first instinct was to blame Beta Jordan for leaving the contact unnamed. Then he remembered giving that order himself. No name, no record, just a number quietly added to his whitelist.","He turned the phone toward Beta Jordan. \"Whose number is this?\"","Beta Jordan glanced at it. \"Sam’s, Alpha. You had me buy the phone, set up the plan, and save your number.\"","\"Then why was he calling all night?\" A chill ran down Alpha Sebastian’s spine. \"Find out what happened.\"","Beta Jordan was already dialing the caregiver.","\"Sam doesn’t get overlooked,\" Alpha Sebastian said sharply. \"Do you understand? Nothing happens to that boy.\"","Because if it did, the last thread connecting him to Eira would be gone.","--","By dusk, the precinct received word that Sam was awake and able to answer questions.","A deputy drove to the hospital and arrived minutes after Kate and Barry came in from Palo Alto. Because Sam was still weak and easily overwhelmed, they entered one at a time.","To everyone’s surprise, Sam did not panic at the uniform. He answered what he could in a quiet, cooperative voice.","Alpha Killian explained that Sam had become terrified when anyone reached toward his head. He also told the deputy how the sight of a white coat had sent the boy into a full panic.","The deputy wrote everything down, thanked them, and left.","At the door, Kate offered him a professional smile.","\"Deputy, please send anything related to Sam Miller’s case directly to me. Kate Morgan. I’m Dr. Crawford’s assistant and Mr.Sterling’s chief of staff.\"","The deputy nodded and left.","Kate and Barry entered the room.","The air smelled of antiseptic.","Eira sat on a low stool beside Sam’s bed, while Alpha Killian stood behind her shoulder, tall and steady. Both turned when the door opened.","Kate and Barry greeted them quietly, then looked toward Sam. Neither approached right away. They waited to see whether he would tense.","Sam did not.","Only then did they move closer. Eira pointed them toward the two empty chairs.","A nurse knocked and stepped inside. She carried Sam’s battered phone on a plastic tray.","\"We tried this first,\" she explained, handing it to Eira. \"It was powered off, so we checked the emergency contact listed in the file. The only number saved in his contacts was this one. He called it repeatedly last night, but no one answered.\"","Her voice softened.","\"When children are given a way to reach someone, the adults need to make sure that number stays active.\"","Eira lowered her eyes. \"You’re right. I understand.\"","\"The phone needs to be charged.\"","\"I’ll get a charger,\" Kate said.","She left and returned a few minutes later with a charging cable and a brand-new phone still in its box.","Eira plugged in Sam’s old phone. When the screen finally lit up, she looked at him, silently asking permission.","Sam gave a small nod.","The newer phone was covered in scratches. A spiderweb crack spread across one corner of the screen. It could have been dropped. It could have been thrown.","Eira opened the contacts.","There was only one number. No name.","The call log showed more than twenty calls from the previous night, placed one after another in the dark hours.","Alpha Sebastian had not answered a single one.","Anger rose hot in Eira’s chest. Then Sam’s hand found hers.","His fingers curled around one of hers.","\"Sis,\" he whispered.","Her anger softened into something painful.","\"You were trying to reach me last night, weren’t you?\"","Sam gave a faint nod.","\"Sis.\"","\"I know.\" She smoothed his hair. \"But that number doesn’t reach me. I’m giving you a new phone. I’ll save my number under ...Sis.’ If you need anything, you call me. Only me. Okay?\"","Sam watched her with tired, uncertain eyes.","Kate handed Eira the new phone. Eira entered her number, called it, and saved the contact in front of him.","Sis.","She placed the phone in Sam’s hand, then stepped into the doorway and answered her own call.","\"Hey, Sam. It’s your sister.\"","Sam tightened his grip on the phone and smiled.","The small smile went straight through Eira’s heart.","She had barely returned to his bedside when the old phone buzzed.","Only two people had access to that number. Alpha Sebastian or Beta Jordan.","Eira’s expression turned cold. She answered and placed the call on speaker.","\"Sam?\" Alpha Sebastian’s voice came through, warm and careful. \"It’s me. Your sister’s husband. I was asleep last night and missed your calls. What’s wrong, buddy? Is there something you need to tell your sister? Take your time. I can pass the message along.\"","The same smooth voice that had lied to adults and frightened children without blinking.","\"Enjoying yourself, Sebastian?\" Eira asked.","A sharp clatter came through the phone, followed by a stunned silence.","\"Eira?\" His voice changed. \"You found Sam?\"","\"Oh, I found him.\" Her tone was colder than the winter wind outside. \"Thanks to you. After you dumped him at that so-called special school, he fell from a second-story window and ended up in surgery.\"","\"Eira, wait. I can explain. I didn’t...\"","She ended the call.","Then she set the old phone aside and pulled out her own.","Alpha Killian watched her scroll to a contact labeled Susan. The corner of his mouth lifted slightly.","\"Susan,\" Eira said. \"I want to file a civil claim against Sebastian Hale and Serena Winthrop. Start the process tonight.\"","\"Tonight?\" Susan asked.","\"I found Sam. So yes. Tonight.\""]},{"number":233,"title":"Chapter 233 One Post That Changed Everything","paragraphs":["Eira ended the call and found everyone in the room watching her.","Kate’s red lips curved into a slow, approving smile. Barry gave her a quiet nod.","\"Congratulations.\"","Alpha Killian looked less impressed. He stood by the window with his arms crossed, his silver-gray eyes fixed on her.","\"Filing the case won’t stop Alpha Sebastian tonight,\" he said. \"The court process takes time. By then, he’ll have lawyers, publicists, and half the city feeding the press his version.\"","A faint trace of mint followed him as he stepped closer.","\"So don’t start with the paperwork,\" he continued. \"Start with the truth. Put it where everyone can see it.\"","Eira understood immediately.","She opened her social media account and typed:","Six weeks ago, I signed a mate-separation agreement with Alpha Sebastian Hale. Two weeks ago, our bond was legally dissolved. We are no longer mated.","She attached two documents, the registered Mate Bond certificate and the official Mate Status Dissolution Certificate.","Alpha Killian liked the post first.","Kate followed, then Barry, Natalie, Miles, Lila , Davies, Beatrice, and Felix.","The comments rushed in almost at once.","Then one comment stood out.","Soren: Is the translation on my end broken?","Eira looked up. \"Soren saw it.\"","\"And?\"","She handed Alpha Killian the phone.","\"Answer him in English,\" he said. \"Make it impossible to misunderstand.\"","Eira switched keyboards and replied directly. There was no translation error. She and Alpha Alpha Sebastian had been divorced for weeks. The gala where she had appeared on his arm had not been voluntary. Alpha Alpha Sebastian had pressured her into attending.","She ended with a polite apology for any confusion.","Soren read the message at home and nearly knocked over his coffee. His first instinct was to call Alpha Sebastian.","Then his phone filled with alerts.","The post had already reached Fiona.","Barry had sent her a screenshot with a short warning:","The boy Alpha Alpha Sebastian used to control Eira has been found. He’s injured, and the school is under investigation. Eira has gone public and is preparing legal action.","If the Carter Group wants to protect its interests, cut Alpha Alpha Sebastian loose before this spreads further.","Alpha Killian noticed the messages on Barry’s screen and said nothing.","Let the leak spread.","Once the Carters withdrew their support, Alpha Sebastian’s access to capital would shrink fast.The board would demand answers. His legal problems would multiply while his public image collapsed.","For the first time, Alpha Sebastian would have no one left to hide behind.","The post reached Hale Tower before his public-relations team could react.","His phone rang again and again. The executive group chat exploded with accusations, screenshots, and questions he could not answer.","The storm had begun.","The Snowmark deal had barely launched. If the Carters pulled their support, Hale Group might survive the fallout.","Alpha Sebastian would not.","Worse, Eira had found Sam. A lawsuit was coming, and Sam was hurt. Whatever fragile hope Alpha Sebastian had been clinging to had finally snapped.","He called Serena.","\"Eira filed,\" he said, his voice flat. \"Get the money ready. Don’t say I didn’t warn you.\"","He ended the call before she could answer.","--","Serena was at the Winthrop estate. She had taken the call in front of Alpha Victor.","Alpha Victor’s face darkened.","\"Serena.\" His voice shook the room. \"This is what you called settled? This is what you said you had handled privately?\"","Her phone nearly slipped from her hand.","\"I don’t know what happened,\" she said quickly. \"I don’t know why Eira suddenly changed her mind.\"","\"You don’t know?\" Alpha Victor’s face had gone pale with rage. \"Then who does?\"","\"Grandfather, I swear, I never thought she would actually file.\"","\"No.\" His disappointment cut deeper than his anger. \"You never thought she could.\"","\"Go to your parents, Serena. They’ve been living off university salaries and research money for years. If they saved anything for you, let them spend it now.\"","The words left Serena speechless.","She turned and stormed out of the estate.","By the time she reached her car, her anger had given way to panic. A sharp pain twisted through her lower abdomen.","She stopped and pressed a hand against her stomach.","Instead of going home, Serena drove straight to the emergency department and asked to be evaluated.","In the exam room, the emergency physician reviewed Serena’s chart.","\"You said you’re about five weeks pregnant?\"","Serena nodded. \"I saw an OB a few weeks ago. They confirmed the pregnancy and did an ultrasound, but I don’t have the records with me.\"","\"That’s okay. We’ll request them from the office. Since you’re having abdominal pain, we’ll run our own tests today.\"","He entered several orders into the computer.","\"We’ll draw blood, check your urine, and repeat the transvaginal ultrasound. The bloodwork will include your blood type and Rh factor, anemia screening, HIV, hepatitis B and C, and syphilis screening.\"","Serena shifted uneasily. \"I thought some of those tests had already been done.\"","\"They may have been. But until we receive your records, we can’t rely on incomplete information. If any result comes back reactive or abnormal, we’ll run follow-up tests before making a diagnosis.\"","The doctor stepped out to place the orders.","Serena sat beneath the harsh fluorescent lights with one hand pressed against her abdomen.","Until then, she had treated the pregnancy like another secret she needed to hide.","Now, one thought drowned out everything else.","[Please, let my baby be okay.]"]},{"number":234,"title":"Chapter 234 Only a Dream","paragraphs":["After the tests were done, Serena drove to her parents’ house with one hand pressed against her lower abdomen.","The emergency doctor told her the hospital would contact her once the remaining lab results were available.","The moment Robert and Jennifer saw her step through the front door, pale and hunched over, they froze.","Robert rushed toward her. \"Did your grandfather find out about the baby?\"","Serena blinked.","\"Did he send you here to get rid of it?\" Robert’s voice cracked. \"God, Serena. Why would you go through something like that alone?\"","\"I knew it.\" Jennifer grabbed a knitted blanket from the sofa and wrapped it around her daughter’s shoulders. Then she hurried to pull the curtains shut. \"That man would sacrifice anyone to protect his reputation. Even his own granddaughter.\"","Robert looked at Serena’s pale face. The fear in her eyes cut him deeply, but his voice dropped.","\"Maybe... maybe it would be easier for everyone if the pregnancy didn’t continue.\"","Serena stared at him as if he had just offered her something rotten.","\"Mom. Dad. I didn’t terminate the pregnancy.\" Her voice shook with disbelief. \"I’m having cramps. That’s all.\"","Both of them went silent.","Then they crowded around her at once.","\"What kind of pain?\"","\"How long has it been going on?\"","\"Did you see a doctor?\"","\"Are you bleeding?\"","\"Enough,\" Serena snapped weakly. \"The ER doctor said it was probably stress.\"","Jennifer guided her to the couch. \"Probably? What kind of answer is that?\"","\"Nothing was seriously wrong with the baby.\" Serena sank down beneath the blanket. \"Grandfather threw me out.\"","Her parents exchanged a worried look.","Serena kept quiet about the lawsuit.","She could not bring herself to say the number out loud. One hundred and eighteen million dollars.","--","At the same time, Eira and Alpha Killian joined Susan on a short video call from Sam’s hospital room.","Eira sat beside the bed, keeping one hand wrapped around Sam’s. Alpha Killian stood behind her, silent and watchful.","\"What if they appeal?\" Eira asked. \"Or ask the court to force mediation?\"","Susan smiled from the screen.","\"Eira, breathe. We built the case with that exact problem in mind. The evidence is already organized, authenticated, and ready to file. We’re requesting emergency relief and moving to block any attempt to delay the matter through mediation.\"","\"So they can’t drag this out?\"","\"They can try,\" Susan said. \"But they won’t get much room to maneuver. The moment the court sees the medical records, the caregiver’s statements, and the school’s failures, their options shrink fast.\"","Eira glanced at Alpha Killian. He looked completely calm.","\"What?\" he asked.","\"Nothing. You’re enjoying this.\"","\"Am I wrong?\"","\"No.\" A tired smile touched her mouth. \"You’re dead-on.\"","Susan nodded. \"Then let’s keep it that way. I’ll file the remaining documents tonight and be there first thing in the morning.\"","The call ended shortly afterward.","It was well past midnight. Eira planned to stay with Sam, and Kate refused to leave her alone. Sam only relaxed when Eira was near him, and Kate was not about to let her friend spend the night in a hospital by herself.","Alpha Killian and Barry headed back to the hotel. The lobby smelled of burnt coffee and industrial floor cleaner.","Barry took one look at Alpha Killian’s exhausted face.","\"Go shower. Get some sleep.\"","\"I’m fine.\"","\"Sure you are.\" Barry grabbed the room key from him. \"You’ll be useless tomorrow if you pass out in the hallway. Eira and Kate aren’t getting any real rest in that room either.\"","For once, Alpha Killian did not argue.","He showered and went straight to bed.","He woke at four in the morning.","The winter sky outside was still black. The image of Eira curled up on a narrow hospital cot came back to him. He washed, dressed, and drove back to the hospital.","Inside the room, Eira was trapped in a nightmare.","Sam was wheeled past her and Alpha Killian, covered in blood. His skin was gray. He was not breathing.","Eira reached for him and tried to scream his name.","No sound came out.","She clawed at her throat, forcing air through her lungs, but her voice was gone.","Alpha Killian caught her as her knees gave way. He pulled her against him and kept saying her name.","She pounded against his back, tears pouring into her mouth.","The gurney carrying Sam rolled toward the morgue.","\"Eira. Wake up.\"","Alpha Killian had just entered the room. He found her thrashing beneath the blanket, her face wet with tears.","Kate was awake too, standing anxiously near the window.","He leaned over Eira and brushed his fingers across her cheek.","\"Eira. Come on. Wake up.\"","Her eyes flew open.","For one terrible second, she could not tell the dream from reality. Then she saw Alpha Killian standing over her, exactly as he had in the nightmare.","She lunged forward and wrapped both arms around him.","\"Killian!\"","Her voice worked."]},{"number":235,"title":"Chapter 235 A Piece of Driftwood","paragraphs":["\"Sam. They can’t take him. I’m sorry. I’m so sorry. This is my fault.\"","Eira’s words broke apart as she began to sob.","Kate’s worried gaze moved between them. Then she quietly stepped into the hall and pulled the door almost closed behind her.","Alpha Killian hesitated before placing one hand against Eira’s back.","\"Eira, listen to me. You were dreaming.\"","She clung to his shirt.","\"It was only a dream. Sam is alive. The surgery worked. He’s right there.\"","\"Where?\"","\"Look at the bed.\"","Eira slowly let go and turned toward Sam.","His chest rose and fell beneath the blanket. The monitor beside him displayed a steady green rhythm.","Eira slid off the cot. Her bare feet hit the cold floor, jolting her fully awake.","\"Thank God,\" she whispered. \"It was only a dream.\"","Alpha Killian pulled a chair behind her.","\"Sit down.\"","She lowered herself into it, still shaking.","He picked up her shoes and crouched in front of her. When he placed one hand around her ankle to help her put them on, his warm skin met hers.","Eira flinched.","\"Hold still.\" His silver-gray eyes lifted to hers. A faint trace of mint lingered between them.","She stared down at him, dazed.","Alpha Killian slipped the shoes onto her feet without a word. Then he pulled another chair beside hers and sat down.","He positioned himself slightly behind her, close enough to notice every change in her expression without crowding her.","Alpha Killian took out his phone and texted Kate.","[Go back to the hotel and get some real sleep. I’ve got Eira. She isn’t alone.]","The room settled into silence. Only the monitor broke it, beeping softly beside Sam’s bed.","Eira watched Sam sleep. Every so often, her gaze drifted toward Alpha Killian.","She could still feel the nightmare. Alpha Killian catching her when her knees gave out. His arms around her. Then the way she had thrown herself against his chest after waking, clinging to him as if he were the only solid thing left in the world.","Like a piece of driftwood in open water.","She hated that thought.","Sebastian had once been her driftwood too.","But Alpha Killian was different.","She glanced at him.","The Alpha of Sterling Pack, a man who controlled boardrooms and closed billion-dollar deals, was sitting in a plastic hospital chair in a small mountain town. He had barely slept, had eaten nothing but vending-machine food, and had not complained once.","Even Eira’s guarded heart softened at the sight.","She lowered her eyes to her shoes.","His firm voice. His gentle hands.","The memory of the night Sebastian had slapped her returned without warning. She had run to a hotel, shaking and humiliated.","The slippers delivered to her room that night had been Alpha Killian’s idea. Eira only learned that later.","They had shared one elevator ride. That was all.","Could Alpha Killian really care that deeply about a stranger?","Outside the window, the sky shifted from black to bruised gray, then slowly brightened into pale gold.","Sam’s eyelids fluttered.","Eira was on her feet before she fully realized he had woken.","\"Sam?\"","He looked up at her, groggy and weak. Then a small smile touched his cracked lips.","\"Hey, Sis.\"","That single word loosened the fist around Eira’s heart.","Only then did she truly believe the nightmare had been nothing more than a dream.","Around noon, Kate called.","\"They cracked,\" Kate said over the phone. \"The whole family folded at the station. Sam’s uncle admitted the missing thumb wasn’t an accident. He broke it on purpose. The district attorney is charging him with felony child abuse.\"","Eira’s stomach twisted. \"And the fall?\"","\"That part is still under investigation. Detectives are heading to the school to find out how Sam ended up over that railing.\"","Eira drove to the station that afternoon.","Sam’s aunt and uncle were being held in a small intake area near the front desk. Nate looked thin and worn, while his wife seemed to have aged ten years overnight. Neither of them looked like the people from the cheerful photographs they had used to convince everyone they were caring for Sam.","The moment Nate’s wife saw Eira, she dropped to her knees.","\"Please.\" She grabbed the hem of Eira’s trousers before a deputy could pull her away. \"You grew up at the Omega Home. You know what it’s like to come from nothing. Please, don’t let them take Nate away. I have three children. Without him, we won’t have enough to eat.\"","\"Nate knew it was wrong,\" she sobbed. \"We know we messed up. We shouldn’t have done that to Sam. Please, have some mercy.\"","Eira looked down at the woman’s blotchy face.","Then her eyes landed on the brand-new down jacket draped over Nate’s wife’s shoulders.","Something bitter twisted in Eira’s chest.","\"You broke that boy’s thumb on purpose,\" she said. Her voice was quiet, but every word landed hard. \"You collected a two-hundred-dollar disability payment for Sam every month while you starved him and hurt him. And now you’re on your knees asking me for mercy?\"","The woman’s sobs grew louder. \"Nate’s going to prison!You need to think about what happens to Sam when we’re gone!\"","\"I am thinking about Sam,\" Eira said. \"I’m going to speak with Miss Gwen about bringing him back to the Omega Home.\"","The woman’s expression changed.","\"If you two hadn’t shown up with custody papers and your so-called family rights, you would never have dragged him away from that home.\" Eira’s eyes hardened. \"He would still be safe. He would still have his whole body. Instead, he’s lying in a hospital bed while doctors try to repair what you did to him.\"","\"Sam getting hurt wasn’t our fault!\" the woman screamed. \"We didn’t send him to that school. Your husband did!\"","The intake area went silent."]},{"number":236,"title":"Chapter 236 Chamomile","paragraphs":["\"Sebastian is not my husband,\" Eira cut in, her voice sharp enough to stop Nate’s wife cold.","Then she lowered it.","\"But don’t worry. He won’t walk away from this clean. Everyone who failed Sam will answer for it.\"","Nate’s wife opened her mouth, but no words came out. Her last bit of confidence drained away.","\"The Omega Home can’t keep him forever,\" she muttered.","Eira looked down at her.","\"As long as I’m alive, Sam will have a safe place to live. If the Omega Home can’t remain his home forever, I’ll make sure we find him somewhere just as safe. He will never be sent back to people like you.\"","She turned before Nate’s wife could reach for her again. A deputy stepped forward and pulled the sobbing woman away from Eira.","Nate’s arrest was already a done deal. The district attorney had no interest in cutting him a break, and neither did Eira.","The school investigation moved even faster than expected. Cases like this usually took weeks to gain momentum. Sam’s case moved in days.","Alpha Killian was the reason.","The truth came out quickly.","Sam was autistic, but he was not helpless or unaware. He spoke very little, especially when he was frightened, but he understood far more than people assumed.","That made him easy to underestimate.","Several boys in his dorm had noticed his new phone. They wanted it. At first, they asked to borrow it. When Sam refused, they started grabbing for it.","That night, they cornered him.","Sam ran.","He climbed onto the outside ledge of a dormitory window and stayed there while the boys shouted at him from inside. The wind cut through his clothes, but he was too afraid to climb back in. He waited until the room went quiet and the other boys fell asleep.","Only then did he try to climb inside.","His foot slipped on the ice-covered sill.","He fell.","The school had failed to provide proper supervision, and the students involved would be held accountable within the limits of the law. Several of them were minors, and some had developmental conditions of their own. The county would decide what charges and consequences were legally possible.","Alpha Killian was not willing to let the school hide behind that uncertainty.","He filed formal complaints against the administration, the facility managers, and the staff responsible for dorm supervision. The complaints covered safety violations, poor staffing, failure to report injuries, and professional misconduct.","He attacked the school from every direction, methodically dismantling its defenses.","Eira watched him from the corner of her eye.","\"What?\" Alpha Killian asked without looking up from his phone.","His silver-gray gaze shifted toward her.","She shook her head. \"Nothing.\"","But her eyes were brighter than they had been in days.","Alpha Killian noticed.","Her relief settled somewhere warm in his chest.","Later, Barry examined Sam and spoke with the hospital team.","\"Once he’s stable enough to travel, we should move him to the city,\" he said. \"The medical center there has better pediatric trauma care, neurological support, and rehabilitation services.\"","\"How soon?\" Eira asked.","\"Possibly in a couple of days. The treating doctors will make the final call. We won’t move him until it’s safe.\"","Eira looked through the glass at Sam’s sleeping face, then nodded.","\"Okay. We’ll take him to the city.\"","Sam spent three days at the small county hospital before the doctors transferred him to a major medical center in the city.","The moment Miss Gwen heard, she drove there herself.","When she saw Sam lying beneath the hospital blanket, bruised and far too small for the bed, her eyes filled with tears.","Deep down, she had known sending him back was a mistake. She had seen it in the couple’s faces when they arrived with custody papers and polished smiles. But she was only the director of the Omega Home.","The paperwork had been legal, and once the court approved the transfer, there had been little she could do.","Eira explained that they wanted Sam returned to the Home.","Miss Gwen nodded at once. \"I’ll handle the paperwork myself.\"","Then she pulled Eira into a gentle hug.","\"You’ve been scared out of your mind, haven’t you, sweetheart?\" she murmured against Eira’s hair. \"Don’t you dare blame yourself. None of this was your fault.\"","Miss Gwen knew her too well. She probably knew Eira had cried somewhere private, in a bathroom or an empty stairwell, where no one could see her fall apart.","\"I know,\" Eira whispered.","Her gaze drifted across the room to Alpha Killian. He stood near the window, quietly giving Kate instructions.","The words he had spoken to her in the dark hospital room had done more than calm her that night. Every time guilt started to close around her throat, his voice came back to her.","This is not your fault.","The memory wrapped around her like a second embrace, keeping the broken pieces of her heart from falling apart.","Alpha Killian felt her watching him. He looked up, ended the conversation with Kate, and crossed the room.","Kate and Barry followed.","\"Miss Gwen, these are two members of my team,\" Alpha Killian said. \"Kate Morgan, my assistant. Barry Wood, my physician.\"","\"It’s a pleasure to meet you,\" Kate said with a warm, professional smile. \"I’ll handle Sam’s arrangements and coordinate with the hospital while he recovers.\"","\"I’ll remain in the city until Sam is cleared to return home,\" Barry added. \"We’ll make sure his follow-up care is arranged before he leaves.\"","Miss Gwen looked from Alpha Killian to Eira. Something softened in her expression. She understood more than either of them said out loud.","\"You’ve all done so much for that boy,\" she said. \"If you’re not too busy, you should visit the Omega Home sometime. I’ll make you a cup of the flower tea the children blend themselves. It’s better than anything you can buy in a store.\"","Alpha Killian tilted his head.","\"Chamomile?\"","Miss Gwen blinked. \"You’ve tried it?\"","\"He has,\" Eira said. \"I made it for him.\"","Alpha Killian’s mouth curved slightly. \"She did.\"","Kate and Barry exchanged a quick look.","There was quiet pride in his voice. Their usually controlled, unshakable Alpha was showing off over a cup of tea.","\"Miss Gwen, the tea can wait,\" Eira said. She glanced at the three exhausted adults. \"These three days have taken a toll. None of them has had a proper shower or a full night’s sleep.\"","Alpha Killian most of all.","They had spent three days in a cramped county hospital. The nearby hotels had been mediocre at best, yet he had not complained once. His phone had kept ringing, and the video calls had never stopped.","Eira had caught him working three times.","Once, he stood at the far end of the hallway with earbuds in, his tall frame outlined by the fluorescent lights. His brow was drawn tight, his jaw hard as stone.","Another time, he had taken an urgent call outside near the flower beds. He spoke in a low voice, then walked quickly toward a quieter corner so no one could overhear him.","The third time, she found him in the car with a laptop open across his knees. The cold blue light cut across half his face, leaving the other side in shadow. Even exhausted, he looked every inch the ruthless CEO who could silence an entire boardroom with one glance.","Those were only the moments she had witnessed. She could only imagine how much Sterling business he had handled when she was not looking.","As soon as the hospital approved Sam’s transfer, Eira booked the best private suite in the city.","She forwarded the reservation details to Kate."]},{"number":237,"title":"Chapter 237 The Girl Who Wouldn’t Eat Bread","paragraphs":["After Alpha Killian and the others left, the hospital room grew quiet.","Only Eira and Miss Gwen remained with Sam. Some color had returned to his face, and his breathing was steadier.","He had not only whispered \"Sis.\" He had also opened his eyes and called for Miss Gwen.","Miss Gwen took Sam’s hand and gently patted it.","\"Sam, sweetheart, the worst is behind you now. From here on out, it’s clear skies. I promise.\"","Eira pulled a chair beside the bed and sat down.","\"You’ve been here almost a week,\" Miss Gwen said softly. \"Shouldn’t you be heading home soon? I’m sure your team is waiting on you.\"","Eira had not exactly been resting. Even from the hospital, she had answered a steady stream of emails and joined several video meetings.","But there were limits to what she could handle from a hospital chair. Classified files could not be sent through ordinary email, and some of her research team’s problems required her to be there in person.","She needed to go back.","\"The day after tomorrow,\" Eira said.","She turned toward Sam and spoke slowly, making sure he understood.","\"Your sister has to go back to work for a little while. But I’ll fly back every weekend to see you. Miss Gwen will stay with you, and Dr. Wood will keep checking on you. You’re going to get better. I promise.\"","Sam gave a quiet, obedient nod.","At the mention of Dr. Wood, Miss Gwen raised her eyebrows. She knew the doctor was one of Alpha Killian’s people.","\"So you and Killian are really just friends?\"","Eira stayed quiet for a moment.","\"Honestly, ...friends’ probably isn’t the right word,\" she admitted. \"I’m his client.\"","Miss Gwen blinked.","\"So you started as business partners, then became friends?\"","Eira did not deny it, but she felt the need to clarify.","\"What I’m saying is that the contractor is helping the client eliminate distractions so she can focus on the project.\"","Miss Gwen stared at her.","Then she smiled.","It was the kind of smile that said, Sure, honey. And I was born yesterday.","Eira pressed her lips together and changed the subject.","\"Is Lainey still at the Omega Home?\"","\"Gone,\" Miss Gwen said. \"The minute you all left, she got a call from her family. She said there was an emergency and caught a flight back.\"","Eira frowned.","\"Did she say what happened?\"","\"No. Just that she had to leave right away.\"","Something about Lainey had never felt right.","\"While she was staying at the Home,\" Eira asked, \"did she do anything unusual? Besides asking about the Home’s history and its notable alumni?\"","Miss Gwen thought for a moment.","\"She refused most of the food,\" she said. \"Wouldn’t touch anything spicy and barely ate the local dishes. Every day, she ordered a car into town for bread and bottled water. She said she couldn’t stomach anything else.\"","\"That is unusual.\"","\"It was.\" Miss Gwen gave a small shrug. \"But everything else? She fit right in. She played with the kids, helped in the kitchen, served lunch, and even taught them how to use her expensive camera. She acted like she’d been part of the Home for years.\"","The uneasy feeling in Eira’s chest grew stronger.","Miss Gwen noticed the deep line between her brows.","\"Is something going on between you two?\" she asked. \"She didn’t come all the way out here because of you, did she?\"","Eira looked up.","\"Don’t forget, she mentioned having a congenital heart condition. The altitude here can be rough on people with heart problems. Yet she still came all the way to the mountains.\"","\"Killian’s mother grew up with Lainey’s father,\" Eira explained. \"Their families have been close for generations.\"","She paused, choosing her words.","\"Lainey has feelings for Killian.\"","Understanding flashed across Miss Gwen’s face. Then her expression clouded with concern.","\"Eira,I don’t know what really happened between you and Sebastian. And I don’t know what’s going on with Killian.\" Miss Gwen swallowed. \"But after hearing all this and learning what kind of family he comes from, I’m scared for you.\"","She reached up and tucked a loose strand of hair behind Eira’s ear.","The worry in her eyes was painfully familiar. It was the fear of a parent who could not protect her child from every danger in the world.","\"Maybe I’m just a small-town woman who hasn’t seen much beyond these hills,\" Miss Gwen continued. \"But when I hear you’re getting involved with people that powerful, my first reaction is fear.\"","Her voice trembled.","\"The world is complicated enough without dragging old family names and bloodlines into it. I’m just the director of Omega Home. I couldn’t even protect you from what happened with Sebastian.\"","She tightened her fingers around Eira’s hand.","\"What happens when you get pulled into their world? What happens when I can’t stand beside you or catch you if you fall?\"","Eira felt every word settle in her chest.","\"Miss Gwen, you don’t have to worry.\" She gave her hand a gentle squeeze. \"My entire life is focused on the project right now. I don’t have the time or energy for anything else.\"","Her lashes lowered.","\"And Killian...\"","His face rose in her mind. His silver-gray eyes. His strong jaw. The quiet certainty in his voice when he had told her in the hospital that Sam’s injuries were not her fault.","Eira stopped before she could finish.","Instead, she held Miss Gwen’s hand and offered her a faint smile.","\"You’re reading too much into it. Even if I weren’t his client, Killian would still help me because I’m his little sister’s best friend. That’s all.\"","Outside in the hallway, Alpha Killian had made it halfway down the hall before turning back and stopping beside the open door. He had heard every word.","He wanted to correct her.","It isn’t because you’re my client.","And it isn’t because you’re Lila’s best friend.","There is something more.","Everything between us is more than that."]},{"number":238,"title":"Chapter 238 The Biscuit","paragraphs":["By the time the conversation in the hospital room faded, Alpha Killian raised a hand and knocked before stepping inside.","Eira turned, puzzled. \"Did you forget something?\"","\"I need you to confirm when you’re flying back to Palo Alto.\"","He could have sent a text. Instead, he had walked all the way back to ask her in person.","For a moment, Eira felt like the one in charge of their arrangement.","\"The day after tomorrow.\"","Alpha Killian gave a quiet hum and nodded to Miss Gwen.","\"Good night.\"","Then he left without looking back.","Eira stared at the door for a moment before picking up her phone. She transferred him a thousand dollars, his agreed daily rate.","A thousand dollars was probably less than what moved through his accounts in a single second.","She kept staring at the payment confirmation until exhaustion pulled her into sleep.","Alpha Killian accepted the transfer.","A car was waiting outside the hospital. He folded his tall frame into the back seat while Barry slid behind the wheel. Kate sat in the passenger seat and glanced at him through the mirror.","Barry caught the dark look on his face.","\"Trouble, Alpha? Did Eira ruffle your fur?\"","Kate tried not to smile.","Alpha Killian met her eyes in the mirror.\"Book my flight back to Palo Alto for the day after tomorrow. You and Barry stay here for two more days. Once Sam is stable and settled, bring him home.\"","\"Got it,\" Kate said.","Barry glanced at him.\"Okay, seriously. What happened?\"","Alpha Killian gave him a sideways look.","They were employer and employee, but they were also friends. After a moment, Alpha Killian told them what he had overheard outside Eira’s room.","The short version was simple. Eira believed he was helping her because she was his client and Lila’s best friend. She had no idea how he really felt.","Barry shrugged. \"If she doesn’t see it, that’s your problem.\"","Alpha Killian’s stare turned colder, but he did not argue.","\"I’m afraid she’ll run.\"","Kate nodded. \"Given everything she’s been through, I wouldn’t bet against it.\"","\"You’ve been playing the long game for a while,\" Barry said. \"It’s not working. She thinks this is all about the contract and Lila. You need to change tactics.\"","Alpha Killian said nothing.","\"Stop hiding behind business,\" Barry continued. \"Make it clear that your feelings have nothing to do with the contract and nothing to do with your sister. She needs to know you want her for herself.\"","Alpha Killian already knew Eira felt something. He had seen it in the way she looked at him, in the way she reached for him when she was frightened.","She simply did not dare believe that he could truly want her.","Barry was right.","It was time to stop waiting.","Alpha Killian remained silent, but the air inside the car seemed to grow warmer.","Over the next two days, Sam continued to improve.","He no longer flinched whenever Barry entered the room. Sometimes, he even mumbled, \"Dr. Wood.\"","Barry had earned that trust.","Watching Sam relax around Barry eased Eira’s mind.","She paid Barry’s medical fee in advance.","Barry glanced at Alpha Killian.","Alpha Killian gave him a small nod.","Barry accepted the payment with a grin. \"Appreciated,Eira.\"","Their flight to Palo Alto was not until the following afternoon, so the group drove to the Omega Home that evening.","Several trucks lined the driveway. Under the floodlights, workers unloaded crates and carried them into the main building.","Miss Gwen watched from the side, pleased but uneasy.","The donation was made in Alpha Killian’s name, but it went far beyond supplies. He was paying for repairs to the heating system, dormitories, kitchen, and medical room. He had also hired two doctors, one for the children’s physical health and another for counseling.","It was generous. Thorough.","Almost too thorough.","\"Killian,\" Miss Gwen said carefully, \"this is far more than we expected.\"","\"The children needed it.\"","\"That still doesn’t explain all of this.\"","Alpha Killian glanced at Eira before answering. \"Consider it an investment in the future.\"","Eira knew the truth. He had chosen the Omega Home because it mattered to her.","Miss Gwen knew it too. Today, the donation looked like a blessing. She only hoped it would never become a debt Eira had to repay.","Alpha Killian seemed to read the concern in both their faces.","\"I’m only building up some good karma,\" he said. \"This isn’t about Eira.\"","His words eased the tension in Eira’s chest. Whatever he truly meant, he had said it in front of everyone. He could not turn around later and demand payment.","Before she could thank him, a group of children came racing around the corner.","\"Eira!\"","Eira crouched and opened her arms. The children crashed into her, piling against her from every direction. She nearly fell backward, but Alpha Killian stepped behind her and steadied her with his legs.","For a second, she stiffened. Then she laughed and wrapped her arms around the children.","They talked over one another about school, games, snacks, and bunk-bed arguments. Eira listened to every story until Miss Gwen called from the hallway.","\"Bedtime!\"","The children groaned.","Eira would leave for the city early the next morning, so she hugged them one by one. Their faces fell when they heard she was leaving again.","\"Ellie, we’ll write you letters,\" one of the older children promised.","\"Deal.\"","A little boy pointed at Alpha Killian. \"Who’s he? Where’s the other guy?\"","\"The other guy was bad,\" Eira said. \"He isn’t allowed here anymore.\"","The children nodded solemnly.","\"No bad guys allowed!\"","\"What about this one?\" another child asked.","Eira stood beside them. \"He’s my friend.\"","\"Your boyfriend?\"","The questions exploded.","\"Are you getting married?\"","\"Will there be cake?\"","\"Do we get candy?\"","\"Can we have a party?\"","Eira opened her mouth, but Kate beat her to it.","\"Of course there’ll be cake and candy at the wedding.\"","The children accepted that immediately and began whispering excitedly.","Barry folded his arms. \"Marriage? Slow down, kids. They don’t even have a date.\"","Miss Gwen started herding everyone toward the dorms.","\"Come on. Say good night.\"","The children shuffled away, waving over their shoulders.","Then a little girl broke away from the group and ran back. She pressed a warm, homemade biscuit into Eira’s palm.","\"Rae. Eat.\"","Her cheeks turned bright red before she spun around and ran after the others.","Eira looked down at the biscuit.","Miss Gwen smiled. \"The kitchen made those this morning. I’d bet she saved it for herself as a late-night snack.\"","Eira’s expression softened.","\"She saved it for me.\"","Alpha Killian’s smooth voice came from above her.","\"Rae?\""]},{"number":239,"title":"Chapter 239 Happy Birthday, Rae","paragraphs":["Eira looked up.","Kate smiled. \"So your nickname is Rae. That’s cute.\"","\"Some of the kids call me that,\" Eira said, tucking a strand of hair behind her ear.","Barry glanced down the cramped hallway. \"Mind if I stay here tonight? I can drive Miss Gwen to the hospital in the morning.\"","Miss Gwen waved him off. \"As long as you don’t mind the accommodations, Doctor Wood.\"","\"I’ve slept in worse,\" Barry said with a grin.","That settled it.","A few minutes later, Barry and Alpha Killian were settled into a tiny dorm room with two sets of bunk beds.","Barry climbed onto the top bunk and stretched out.","\"This takes me back to my UCLA days. Bet you never lived like this, Killian. A guy like you probably had a private wing before he could walk.\"","Alpha Killian ignored him. He leaned against the railing and opened his phone.","Barry caught a glimpse of the screen as Alpha Killian changed one of his contacts.","Rae.","Then he locked his phone and looked at Barry.","\"Look into Sam’s condition. Find out what support he’ll need for communication and daily care.\"","Barry’s expression grew serious. \"There’s no magic fix for autism, if that’s what you mean. But speech therapy, occupational therapy, and the right specialists could help him communicate more easily. I can arrange a full evaluation.\"","\"Send me the bill.\"","\"Like you’ve ever let me pay for anything,\" Barry muttered.","Alpha Killian’s stare turned cold.","Barry sighed, then added, \"While I’m here, I could ask around about Eira. She grew up in the system, right? Maybe we can find out where she came from.\"","Alpha Killian’s expression changed at once.","Barry lowered his voice. \"Her family history might explain a few things.\"","After a long pause, Alpha Killian said, \"Find out. Quietly.\"","\"Got it.\"","--","The next morning, Eira was up early, helping serve breakfast in the dining hall.","She was halfway through the line when Alpha Killian walked in.","A little boy spotted him and waved. \"Morning, Mr. Sterling!\"","Alpha Killian gave him a brief nod. \"Morning.\"","The boy beamed and turned to the others. \"He said good morning!\"","Within seconds, more children were calling out to him.","\"Morning, Mr. Sterling!\"","\"Hey, Killian!\"","\"Morning!\"","Alpha Killian tried to answer them all, but the greetings quickly turned into a wall of noise.","\"All right, give him a break,\" Eira called. \"Go eat before your breakfast gets cold.\"","The children laughed and scattered.","Alpha Killian stopped in front of her.","\"What are you having?\" Eira asked. \"I’ll fix you a plate.\"","\"I’ll wait. I’ll have whatever you’re having.\"","She gave him a long look. \"Then go find a seat.\"","Alpha Killian lowered his tall frame into a tiny blue plastic chair. His knees nearly reached the table, and the chair looked ridiculous beneath him. Still, he sat straight-backed and serious, as if he were in a board meeting instead of a crowded dining hall.","Eira finished serving, removed her apron, and carried two bowls of oatmeal to the table. She added brown sugar and berries to hers, then pushed the second bowl toward him.","Alpha Killian took the spoon and glanced at her.","\"Do I pass inspection?\"","\"Barely.\"","He took a bite.","Outside, snow drifted past the frosted windows. Inside, the room smelled of cinnamon, coffee, and warm toast.","Alpha Killian looked at her.","\"Thank you, Rae.\"","The nickname sounded unexpectedly intimate in his low voice.","Eira froze with her spoon halfway to her mouth. She looked up into his silver-gray eyes, then quickly lowered her gaze.","\"Mm.\"","They finished breakfast in comfortable silence.","A little later, Kate drove them to the airport.","--","Palo Alto.","Lila picked them up herself. The moment she saw Eira, her face lit up, and she started talking before Eira had even closed the car door.","\"Okay, so this morning I drove Mrs. Jones over to Ten Ashford Lane to help her clean the place from top to bottom...\"","Alpha Killian’s eyes narrowed when he recognized the car.","So that was why Lila had been driving it so often. She had been spending a lot of time at Ten Ashford Lane.","\"Get in, Eira,\" Lila said brightly, throwing open the passenger door. \"My brother can take the back seat. He knows how to open a car door.\"","Alpha Killian said nothing. He slid into the back.","Lila pulled away from the curb and headed toward Southridge Estates.","Eira glanced over her shoulder. \"So, what did I miss while I was gone?\"","\"Where do I even start?\" Lila said. \"That post of yours blew up Sebastian’s entire family. Not figuratively. It was a full-blown detonation.\"","Eira raised an eyebrow.","\"Sebastian is out at Hale Group. They didn’t exactly fire him. They had a very serious conversation, and then he suddenly resigned.\" Lila made air quotes with her fingers. \"No severance. No golden parachute. Nothing.\"","Eira’s mouth curved slightly.","\"Since then, the Hale household has been a total shitshow. Oh, and Isabella came looking for you. She didn’t even make it past the property line. One of the dogs chased her off, and apparently, she hit the ground hard.\"","\"Isabella fell?\" Eira asked.","\"Face-first, according to Mrs. Jones.\" Lila grinned. \"I didn’t see it myself, so I can’t swear to it. But honestly, I would’ve paid good money for the replay.\"","A quiet laugh escaped Eira."]},{"number":240,"title":"Chapter 240 The Fall of an Alpha","paragraphs":["Three days earlier, Alpha Sebastian had been summoned before the board.","He descended the glass staircase at Hale Group and crossed the marble lobby with Jordan close behind. Conversations died around them.","Employees looked away whenever Alpha Sebastian glanced over, then leaned together and whispered behind raised hands.","He did not know how much they had pieced together. He knew one thing for sure. Everyone had heard that Soren, Snowmark’s director, had threatened to walk away from the contract.","Hale Group was not built on one deal, but Snowmark was the biggest international project of the year, possibly the next two. Alpha Sebastian had led it from the beginning.","First, he had lost the processor bid. Then Dr. Shaw’s patent had slipped out of his hands. Now Snowmark was threatening to leave.","Every failure led back to him.","Some employees said Alpha Sebastian was cursed. Others whispered that he had crossed the wrong person. But the rumor spreading fastest was far uglier.","Alpha Sebastian had taken a mate and then dissolved the bond. That alone would not have been shocking. Packs ended relationships all the time. The scandal was what came next.","He had betrayed his Luna during the bond and funneled a fortune to another woman.","Jordan had heard the whispers in the break room more than once. He always shut them down immediately. He could ignore the jokes about bad luck, but the moment anyone insulted Eira, his temper snapped.","That only made the rumors sound more believable.","Everyone on the floor watched as Alpha Sebastian and Jordan left the building, both men wearing grim expressions.","\"Do you think they’re firing him?\" someone whispered.","The word spread through the office like a cold draft.","Then everyone returned to work. No one wanted to be caught gossiping when the axe finally fell.","Inside the car, Alpha Sebastian leaned against the seat and closed his eyes.","Jordan sat beside him, tense and pale. But when he saw how still Alpha Sebastian looked, his own fear faded into something heavier.","Hopelessness.","Alpha Sebastian already knew the meeting was a formality. He was being escorted to the gallows.","The board meeting took place in Carter Group’s top-floor conference room. Every director was present, along with Alpha Carter and his two children, Fiona and Finn.","The directors attacked him from every side. They blamed his personal conduct for the failed deals and the Snowmark crisis.","Alpha Sebastian caught one word.","\"Crisis,\" a director snapped. \"You nearly lost Snowmark.\"","Nearly.","Alpha Sebastian looked toward Alpha Carter. \"So the contract is still active?\"","\"We renegotiated the terms to keep Snowmark at the table,\" Alpha Carter said. \"That means Hale Group accepted major concessions.\"","A director slammed his palm against the table. \"Do you understand what you’ve cost us? Once your hearing becomes public, you’ll drag both companies through the mud.\"","Alpha Sebastian remained calm.","\"What has the board decided?\" he asked. \"Say it plainly.\"","The director turned to Alpha Carter. \"Terminate him today.\"","Alpha Carter held Alpha Sebastian’s silver gaze.","\"Resign,\" he said. \"Do it on your own terms.\"","A murmur moved through the room.","Alpha Sebastian understood what Alpha Carter was offering. Not mercy. One last scrap of dignity.","He nodded. \"Fine.\"","As the directors began to leave, Alpha Sebastian turned back.","\"Who takes over Hale Group?\"","\"That is no longer your concern,\" one director said.","Alpha Sebastian ignored him and looked at Finn. \"If Finn takes over, keep Jordan. I’m under a two-year non-compete, so he isn’t a threat. But he knows every part of this company.\"","Finn studied him. Alpha Sebastian was ruthless, but he still protected his people.","Alpha Carter gave a slight nod.","\"Done,\" Finn said.","--","That afternoon, an email reached every employee at Hale Group.","Alpha Sebastian Hale has resigned for personal reasons.","The company was in chaos.","By the time Alpha Sebastian reached Number Eleven at Southridge Estates, he was carrying a cardboard box filled with the few things he had taken from his office.","His family had gathered in the living room. Even the longtime housekeeper had stayed, hovering near the kitchen as if the house itself might collapse.","Alpha Sebastian stepped inside.","His father’s face went pale. \"You resigned?\"","Luna Margaret and Isabella shot to their feet. They did not seem to believe it until Alpha Sebastian gave a tired nod.","\"This morning. The announcement has already gone out.\"","\"Did they force you out, or did you walk?\" Luna Margaret demanded.","Alpha Sebastian pinched the bridge of his nose and dropped onto the sofa. Exhaustion showed in every line of his face.","\"They told me to resign.\"","\"They told you, and you actually did it?\" Isabella stared at him. \"Are you out of your mind?\"","\"Are you?\" Alpha Sebastian snapped. \"I’m too tired to explain this twice.\"","Alpha Roger stepped in before the argument could grow.","\"Given the situation, resigning was the only way he could leave with any dignity.\"","Isabella’s mouth twisted. \"This is Serena’s fault. Eira is suing her, right? Then make Serena return every dollar. Eira can split the money with you. It was yours in the first place.\"","Alpha Sebastian stood.","\"Even if Eira recovers every dollar, none of it is coming to me. Let it go.\"","\"Why not?\"","\"In a normal bond dissolution, I might have been entitled to a share.\" His jaw tightened. \"But if the court rules that I violated my obligations to Eira, the situation changes. She could recover everything. I would have no legal claim to it.\"","The color drained from Isabella’s face.","\"So we cannot count on that money,\" she whispered.","\"Stop counting money that isn’t yours,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"I don’t have the right to touch it anymore.\"","Isabella burst into tears and grabbed Luna Margaret’s arm.","\"Mom, I don’t want to end up like those people who have to work a regular job.\"","Alpha Sebastian gave her a cold look. \"And why exactly can’t you work? Do you honestly think you’re some kind of heiress?\"","\"Enough,\" Luna Margaret cut in. \"Both of you.\"","Isabella only cried harder.","Alpha Roger rubbed his temple. \"That’s enough. You’re giving me a headache.\"","He looked at Alpha Sebastian, his anger mixed with disappointment.","\"We all played a part in this. Every one of us. But Serena caused the deepest damage.\" His voice hardened. \"You bonded with Eira. So why did you keep running after Serena? Now she has drained your money, wrecked your career, and left this family cleaning up the mess.\"","Alpha Sebastian lowered his head.","For once, he had no defense.","\"Dad. Mom. I’m sorry.\"","Luna Margaret turned and walked away before he could see her cry. Alpha Roger rested a hand on Alpha Sebastian’s shoulder.","\"I’ll check on your mother. Business comes and goes. If you’re still standing, you still have another day.\"","After his parents left, Isabella wiped her face.","\"Sebastian, what if we asked Eira for help? Do you think she would give us some of the money she gets from Serena?\"","His headache throbbed behind his eyes.","\"I don’t know.\"","\"Then I’ll ask her myself.\"","Isabella rushed to Number Nine. Two large dogs patrolled the property behind the gate. She grabbed a pair of landscaping stones and stepped closer.","\"Eira!\" she shouted. \"It’s me, Isabella!\"","The dogs charged.","Isabella threw a stone, but it only made them bark harder. She stumbled backward and hit the ground twice, bruising both knees.","She scrambled away from the gate and glared at the house.","\"This is all Serena’s fault,\" she muttered. \"Every last bit of it.\""]},{"number":241,"title":"Chapter 241 Collecting a Debt","paragraphs":["The next morning, Isabella drove straight to The Celestia Residences, determined to find Serena.","She stormed into the lobby wearing oversized sunglasses and a designer coat she could no longer afford.","At the front desk, she gave the doorman Serena’s name and tower number.","Before she could finish, he offered her a polite, practiced smile.","\"Are you here about the penthouse listing, ma’am? The unit just went on the market.\"","Isabella blinked. \"The listing?\"","\"Yes. The real estate agent put up the notice this morning. If you’re interested, I can give you their number.\"","\"I’m not here to buy the place.\" Isabella’s voice rose. \"I’m looking for Serena Winthrop.\"","The doorman’s smile faded slightly. \"I’m sorry, ma’am. I can’t confirm whether she’s home.\"","\"She’s selling the penthouse?\"","\"I only know that the unit is listed.\"","That was enough.","Serena was liquidating everything. The apartment, the car, the jewelry, anything that could be turned into cash.","Isabella turned on her heel and marched out.","If Serena was not hiding in her apartment, she was probably at the Winthrop estate, sheltered behind Alpha Victor and the family name.","Twenty minutes later, Isabella stood outside the estate gates, pounding on the iron bars.","\"Serena!\" she shouted. \"Get out here! You owe my brother every dollar he ever gave you!\"","A guard approached. \"Ma’am, step away from the gate.\"","\"Tell Serena to come outside!\"","The shouting drew people from the house. Within minutes, the entire estate was in an uproar.","Alpha Victor appeared at the front entrance, his face tight with humiliation.","\"Remove her,\" he ordered.","Two guards moved toward the gate, but Olivia stepped out before they could reach Isabella. Serena’s aunt wore a silk robe over neatly pressed clothes, as if she had been interrupted halfway through breakfast.","She gave Isabella a cool, almost amused look.","\"And what exactly will throwing her out accomplish?\" Olivia asked. \"She’ll come back tomorrow and make the same scene. At the end of the day, Serena is the one who owes the money. Let me deal with this.\"","Alpha Victor’s jaw tightened. He clearly hated the spectacle, but after a long pause, he motioned for the guards to stand down.","Olivia walked to the gate and stopped a few feet away from Isabella.","\"Making a scene here will not get you paid,\" she said. \"Serena has her own family, you know. She’s staying with her parents.\"","\"Then give me their address.\"","Olivia’s smile sharpened.","\"Gladly.\"","She recited the address and watched Isabella enter it into her phone.","\"Your niece is hiding behind her parents,\" Isabella said.","\"Then you should take your complaint to the people who are sheltering her.\"","Isabella turned and stormed back to her car.","Across town, she drove to an older, quieter neighborhood lined with oak trees and modest two-story homes.","Serena’s parents’ house wasn’t luxurious, but it was warm and well maintained. A brass wreath hung on the front door, and potted evergreens sat on either side of the porch.","Isabella climbed the steps and pounded on the door.","\"Who is it?\"","Serena opened it.","The moment she saw Isabella standing there, the color drained from her face.","Of all the people who could have found her, Isabella was the worst. She had the loudest voice, the sharpest temper, and no sense of shame when money was involved.","\"How did you find me?\" Serena demanded.","She stepped outside and pulled the door shut behind her. Her eyes flicked toward the living room window.","She could not let her parents hear this.","For the past few days, she had been hiding inside their home while the pressure closed in around her.","After the hospital visit, she had finally confessed the truth.","She owed a staggering $118 million.","Robert had slapped her across the face.It was the first time he had ever hit her.","Jennifer had not defended Serena. She had stood beside the kitchen table with tears sliding down her cheeks, unable to find a single word.","No one had slept that night.","By morning, her parents had emptied every account and gathered every document they could find. Bank cards, property deeds, investment statements, jewelry, and the small savings they had built for Serena’s future covered the kitchen table.","Even if they sold both houses, they would barely raise a million dollars.","It was not even a fraction of what Serena might owe.","Both of her parents were tenured professors. They had spent their entire lives building respectable careers. Asking colleagues for money to cover their daughter’s affair and unpaid debts would destroy their reputation as completely as it would destroy their finances.","Serena had heard every desperate phone call.","That was why she had spent the past week acting like the obedient daughter. She cooked when her mother asked, stayed quiet during family meals, and apologized whenever her father entered the room.","No one dared mention the pregnancy anymore.","The baby had become the one subject they avoided completely.","Now Isabella was standing on their porch, ready to expose everything.","Serena grabbed her wrist.","\"Keep your voice down,\" she hissed. \"Come around back.\"","Isabella yanked her arm free.","\"What’s wrong? Afraid your mommy and daddy will find out that creditors are knocking?\" Her voice rose. \"Maybe you should have thought about that before you slept with a married man and blew through his money!\"","The words echoed through the narrow entryway.","The houses in the neighborhood sat close together, and Serena’s parents knew nearly everyone on the block.","One loud argument was all it would take for the neighbors to hear about it, and by morning, the whole block would know.","Serena slapped a hand over Isabella’s mouth.","\"Shut up,\" she whispered fiercely. \"I’m warning you.\"","Isabella glared at her and nodded.","Serena slowly loosened her grip.","For one second, she thought Isabella might listen.","Then Isabella shouted, \"Pay up, you little homewrecker!\"","Her voice shook the walls.","Click.","The front door opened behind them.","Robert and Jennifer stood in the doorway, both of them pale. Robert’s shoulders were rigid, while Jennifer held one hand against her chest.","Serena’s stomach dropped.","\"Dad, Mom, it’s not what you think.\"","Robert looked from his daughter to Isabella.","\"Whatever this is, bring it inside,\" he said quietly.","Isabella gave Serena a smug smile and walked into the house as if she had been invited.","Serena followed, her hands clenched at her sides.","The Winthrop home was older than the Celestia penthouse, but it was spacious and comfortable. Family photographs lined the hallway. Books filled the shelves. A pot of coffee sat untouched on the kitchen counter, its bitter smell hanging in the air.","Jennifer closed the door and faced Isabella.","\"Who are you?\"","\"Isabella Hale,\" she said. \"Sebastian’s sister.\"","Jennifer’s face tightened at the name.","\"What do you want?\" she asked.","\"I’m here about the money Serena took from my brother.\" Isabella replied."]},{"number":242,"title":"Chapter 242 The Price of Silence","paragraphs":["\"Legally, Sebastian has no claim to it now,\" Jennifer replied evenly. \"Any money recovered through the lawsuit belongs to Eira. We are already trying to gather what we can. If you want to make a claim, speak to Eira’s attorney. Showing up here and threatening us is harassment. I can call the police.\"","Isabella laughed.","\"Go ahead. Call them.\" She stepped closer. \"I’ll stand in the hallway with a bullhorn and tell every neighbor that your precious daughter slept with a married man, burned through his money, and is now being sued by the wife. Let’s see how proud you feel when the whole neighborhood knows exactly what your daughter has done.\"","Jennifer’s neck stiffened. No one had ever spoken to her that way.","Robert slipped an arm around his wife’s shoulders. His face had turned dark with anger.","Serena grabbed Isabella’s wrist. \"Didn’t you hear her? Whatever money is recovered belongs to Eira, not you. Take it up with her.\"","Isabella pulled free.","\"So you’re not paying me?\"","\"We don’t have the money.\"","\"Then I’ll tell everyone.\"","Robert and Jennifer exchanged a frightened look. They knew Isabella was reckless enough to do it.","Serena’s face tightened with desperation.","\"Fine. Go ahead and scream.\" She placed a hand over her lower abdomen. \"But remember, Isabella, I’m carrying your brother’s child. If anything happens to this baby because you keep attacking me, that will be on you.\"","Isabella’s eyes dropped to Serena’s stomach.","\"Oh, right. I almost forgot. You’re pregnant with my brother’s little bastard.\"","\"Isabella.\" Serena’s voice shook.","\"Sebastian and Eira are divorced,\" Serena said. \"My baby is not a bastard.\"","\"No ring. No father. That’s what people will call it.\" Isabella’s voice turned cruel. \"Go ahead and have the baby. See what the other kids say when they find out he’s growing up with no father. A little stray with only a mother and no...\"","\"Shut up!\"","Serena slapped her across the face.","For one second, the room went completely still.","Then Isabella lunged. She grabbed a fistful of Serena’s hair and yanked hard.","\"You crazy little...\"","Robert caught Isabella around the shoulders while Jennifer pulled Serena away. The three of them stumbled into the entryway, knocking over a small side table.","\"This is my house!\" Robert shouted. \"Get your hands off her!\"","Isabella fought against his grip, still cursing, but Jennifer managed to push Serena behind her.","Then Serena doubled over.","The anger drained from her face.","A sharp pain twisted through her lower abdomen, stronger than before. She pressed both hands against her stomach and sucked in a breath.","\"Dad...\"","Robert released Isabella and turned toward her.","\"Mom, I need a hospital.\" Serena’s voice broke. \"Something’s wrong.\"","Jennifer grabbed her phone with shaking hands and called 911.","The pain came in another wave. Serena bent forward, her face turning pale.","Isabella stopped struggling.","This was no longer a fight. If the pregnancy ended, everyone would blame her for starting the confrontation.","When the ambulance arrived, paramedics helped Serena onto the stretcher. Robert and Jennifer climbed in beside her.","Isabella stood on the sidewalk, shaken and furious. Then she flagged down a cab and followed them to Mercy General.","At the hospital, Serena was taken to the emergency department and then moved to the obstetric unit.","The same physician who had seen her during her first visit came in to evaluate her.","The moment he heard about the worsening abdominal pain, his expression tightened.","\"Most of your previous results are already here,\" he said. \"Your CBC, quantitative beta-hCG, blood type, Rh factor, urine test, and initial ultrasound have all been recorded.\"","Serena pressed a hand against her lower abdomen. \"Then why does it hurt so much?\"","\"Because your symptoms have changed, and we need to find out why.\"","He scrolled through the chart.","\"Your HIV, hepatitis B and C, and syphilis screens were sent to an outside lab. They’re still pending, but there’s no reason to repeat them today. We’ll review those results when they come back.\"","Serena swallowed. \"What are you going to do now?\"","\"We’ll repeat the transvaginal ultrasound and compare it with the last scan. We need to check the location of the pregnancy and look for any sign of bleeding or another complication. Depending on what we see, we may repeat your CBC or beta-hCG level.\"","\"You think something is wrong with the baby?\"","\"I’m not saying that. I’m saying worsening abdominal pain in early pregnancy needs to be evaluated in person.\"","He entered the order into the computer.","\"I’ll also ask the OB team to review the images. If the results are reassuring, we’ll talk about discharge and follow-up. If anything looks concerning, we’ll keep you here for observation.\"","Robert and Jennifer nodded at once.","\"Do whatever you need to do,\" Robert said.","After the nurses settled Serena into a hospital room, her parents stepped out to speak with the doctor.","Serena reached for her phone and called Alpha Sebastian.","He answered after several rings.","\"Serena?\"","\"Isabella came after me today.\" Serena made her voice tremble. \"She frightened me so badly that I started having severe cramps. I’m at the hospital.\"","There was a pause.","\"Are you bleeding?\"","\"Not yet. But I’m scared.\" She pressed a hand to her stomach. \"Sebastian, this is your baby too. Please come sit with me.\"","He said nothing.","\"She called our child a fatherless stray,\" Serena whispered. \"She said no one in your family wants this baby.\"","The silence on the line grew longer.","Then Alpha Sebastian’s voice came through, low and tired.","\"I’m on my way.\"","A faint smile touched Serena’s lips.","\"Thank you.\"","She ended the call just as Isabella entered the room.","Isabella had heard enough. Disgust twisted her face.","\"Unbelievable. Let me save you the heartbreak. Even if my brother comes, he isn’t coming because he wants this pregnancy. He’s coming to tell you it’s over. Mom already told him yesterday. We don’t want this baby.\"","Serena’s pupils tightened.","Then she slowly lifted her chin.","\"Whether this baby stays or goes is not your decision. It’s not your mother’s decision, either. It’s my body and my choice.\"","\"You’re only keeping the pregnancy to trap my brother,\" Isabella shot back. \"And don’t flatter yourself. A woman like you is not guaranteed a healthy baby just because she wants one.\"","Serena’s hand tightened around the blanket.","\"If you have so much to say, wait until Alpha Sebastian gets here and say it to his face. Stop hiding behind insults when it’s just the two of us.\"","\"You think he’s going to choose you?\"","\"I think you’re terrified he won’t choose your family.\"","The two women glared at each other until Robert and Jennifer returned."]},{"number":243,"title":"Chapter 243 A Shrinking Kingdom","paragraphs":["By the time Alpha Sebastian reached Mercy General, Robert and Jennifer had stepped out to speak with the billing office.","Isabella remained in the room, perched on the vinyl couch beneath the window. Her lacquered nails tapped against her phone as she scrolled.","She had refused to leave.","The Hale family was already drowning. Alpha Sebastian had lost his job, their accounts were nearly empty, and Serena owed more than a hundred million dollars.","If she managed to take another cent from Alpha Sebastian, the entire family could lose everything.","\"Look who finally showed up,\" Isabella said without looking up.","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened. \"What the hell are you doing here?\"","\"Collecting what she owes you.\" Isabella lifted her eyes toward Serena. \"She cost you your job. The least she can do is write you a check.\"","\"Isabella,\" he warned.","\"Back when she was overseas, you wired her money without asking questions. Now you’re broke, and she suddenly can’t spare a dime.\" Isabella gave Serena a cold smile. \"That tells us who really loved who, doesn’t it?\"","Serena’s jaw tightened. She ignored Isabella and turned to Alpha Sebastian, her green eyes filling with tears.","\"The doctor said stress isn’t good for the baby.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s gaze dropped to her stomach. After a long pause, he looked at his sister.","\"Go home, Isabella.\"","She crossed her arms and sank deeper into the couch.","\"No.\"","Alpha Sebastian did not argue. He simply turned back to Serena.","She curled her fingers into the blanket. \"What did she mean about your job?\"","He stood beside the bed, his expression hard and distant.","\"Alpha Carter asked me to resign. The announcement went out this morning. I’m finishing the handover with Finn, and then I’m done at Hale Group.\"","Serena’s face went pale.She lowered her gaze. \"Sebastian, I’m sorry.\"","Isabella snorted, but Serena ignored her.","\"It’s not the end of the world,\" Serena said quickly. \"You have a strong reputation. Headhunters will be calling. Another Pack will hire you as a CEO within weeks.\"","\"I signed a two-year non-compete.\"","The hope vanished from her face.","No job. No income. And more than a hundred million dollars in debt.","\"Then you can work in another industry,\" she said, forcing the words out. \"Something related to technology. You could consult, or join a private firm...\"","\"We’ll see.\"","His voice stopped her.","\"You know my situation now,\" he continued. \"You’re barely holding your own life together. Are you sure you still want to have this baby?\"","Serena stared at him. \"What are you saying?\"","Isabella answered before he could.","\"He’s saying that keeping the baby is your choice. But the Hales are not paying for it, raising it, or cleaning up another financial disaster. If you want this child, you’ll have to support it yourself.\"","Alpha Sebastian shot her a warning look.","She finally fell silent.","Tears rolled down Serena’s cheeks.","\"This is our child,\" she whispered. \"You said you only wanted children I carried. This baby exists because you agreed to it. How can you suddenly act like he means nothing?\"","Alpha Sebastian said nothing.","\"Things went wrong for all of us,\" Serena continued, both hands covering her abdomen. \"But this baby is innocent. We can’t punish the baby for what we did.\"","Alpha Sebastian remained unreadable.","\"They’re repeating the ultrasound and checking my bloodwork because the pain got worse,\" she said softly. \"Please wait for the results. Hear what the doctor says before you decide anything.\"","Silence filled the room.","Finally, Alpha Sebastian said, \"Fine.\"","Serena released a shaky breath.","\"My parents have been running themselves into the ground because of me.\" She wiped her cheeks. \"Will you stay tonight? Just until the doctor comes back with the results?\"","Alpha Sebastian pulled a chair beside the window and sat down.","Outside, the city lights flickered on one by one.","He remembered how Eira used to leave a single lamp burning for him, no matter how late he came home. The moment he walked through the door, the pressure of the day seemed to disappear.","Alpha Sebastian closed his eyes.","He missed her so badly it hurt.","And he had been the one who pushed her away. He had turned the woman who loved him into his enemy with his own hands.","Serena texted her parents, telling them to go home and get some rest. Alpha Sebastian had arrived, and she was no longer alone.","Isabella watched her brother pull a chair beside the window. She knew exactly what Serena planned to do next. She would wait until the room was quiet, cry a little, and keep working on Alpha Sebastian until he opened his wallet again.","Isabella grabbed her coat.","At the door, she stopped and looked back at her brother.","\"Sebastian, one thing before I go.\" Her voice turned cold. \"If she starts crying and convinces you to pay her debt to Eira, remember who you’re helping.\"","Serena’s fingers tightened around the blanket.","\"She drugged Eira,\" Isabella continued. \"So picture this. You hand Serena the money, she passes it straight to Eira, and Eira finds out you helped the woman who hurt her.\"","Serena nearly came off the bed.","Isabella had found the exact place to press. She had used Eira’s name like a blade.","Then she opened the door and walked out.","The room fell silent.","Serena lowered her head. Tears slipped down her cheeks, one after another, without a sound.","He said nothing. He only pushed the tissue box across the blanket.","The door opened again.","The emergency physician stepped inside, followed by a nurse. He glanced at Serena, then at Alpha Sebastian.","\"Are you the father?\"","Alpha Sebastian nodded.","The doctor’s expression hardened.","\"She is in the early stages of pregnancy, and this is already her second visit for abdominal pain. She has no established prenatal records, and she has been under serious emotional stress.\"","Alpha Sebastian lowered his eyes.","\"That’s my fault,\" he said quietly. \"The situation has been complicated.\"","\"Complicated does not change the medical risks.\" The doctor checked the monitor and then looked back at him. \"She needs proper prenatal care, follow-up with an OB, and a stable environment. If the pain gets worse, if she has bleeding, dizziness, fainting, or shoulder pain, she needs immediate attention.\"","Serena wiped her cheeks.","\"We’re still deciding whether to continue the pregnancy,\" Alpha Sebastian said.","The doctor studied both of them for a moment.","\"That is a personal decision, but you need accurate medical advice before making it. You are still early enough that you have options, but those options depend on your health, the ultrasound findings, and how far along the pregnancy is. Do not delay speaking with an obstetrician or a qualified provider.\"","He turned toward the door, then paused.","\"And whatever you decide, make the decision together and without threatening or pressuring each other. Her health comes first.\"","Alpha Sebastian stood. \"We understand.\"","The doctor gave him a firm look.","\"I hope you do.\""]},{"number":244,"title":"Chapter 244 The Verdict Approaches","paragraphs":["Serena knew it now. Deep down, Alpha Sebastian truly did not want the baby.","Cold panic spread through her chest.","The child had been her last piece of leverage, the one thing that might keep Alpha Sebastian opening his wallet and pulling her out of the financial disaster swallowing her whole.","She turned toward him.","\"Sebastian,\" she whispered, making her voice tremble. \"I can’t calm down. Would you lie beside me for a while? Just hold me.\"","He sat in the chair near the window with his eyes closed. Neon from the city painted sharp shadows across his tired face.","\"Is your stomach hurting again?\"","\"My mind won’t shut off.\"","\"Yeah.\" His mouth twisted bitterly. \"Mine either.\"","Serena studied his profile. \"Do you blame me for everything?\"","\"We’re already standing in the wreckage,\" he said. \"What good would blaming each other do now?\"","Alpha Sebastian had spent months feeling one disaster after another crash into him. Every blow had tightened the pressure in his chest.","Now the worst had happened. His career was gone, his reputation was damaged, and Eira had become his enemy. Strangely, the panic had faded. Once the disaster was fully in front of him, there was nothing left to fear.","Serena had no such calm.","Alpha Sebastian had lost his career. She had lost her reputation and gained a debt of more than a hundred million dollars. She was the one facing the real financial ruin.","The baby might keep Alpha Sebastian paying for a little longer. But if that failed, who else could she turn to?","Vincent was useless. Nothing had ever happened between them.","Ryan Sullivan was different.","Sullivan Enterprises was smaller, but it was profitable. Serena was about to join its research division, which would make asking Ryan for money look less suspicious. She could call it an advance, an investment, or support for the new project.","The plan steadied her nerves, but sleep still would not come.","She slipped out of the hospital bed and crossed the small room. Then she pressed herself against Alpha Sebastian’s chest.","He jerked upright.","\"What the hell are you doing?\"","\"I feel safe when I’m close to you.\"","She lifted her face and tried to kiss him.","Alpha Sebastian turned away at once.","\"Serena. Don’t.\"","\"Before the divorce, we did this all the time.\" She stepped back, hurt flashing across her face. \"Why is it suddenly off-limits now?\"","\"Because I told you what we had was a mistake. I’m not going to keep making it.\"","Tears filled her eyes.","\"You and Eira already...\"","\"Don’t.\" He stood so quickly the chair scraped against the floor. \"I don’t need you to remind me.\"","He headed for the door.","\"Sebastian, wait.\" Panic cracked through her voice. \"They’re running more tests. I can’t do this alone.\"","He stopped with one hand on the doorframe.","\"I’m going outside for some air.\"","He stayed away long enough for Serena to start watching the clock.","A nurse finally returned to take her for the transvaginal ultrasound. Alpha Sebastian came back and followed them to the imaging department.","The scan was uncomfortable, and Serena gripped the sheet while the technician worked. Afterward, she complained of dizziness and pressed gauze against her arm while Alpha Sebastian steadied her by the shoulder.","To anyone watching, they looked like a devoted couple.","Only Serena knew he was standing beside her out of duty.","The ultrasound showed no immediate cause for concern.","The doctor also told Serena that the HIV, hepatitis B and C, and syphilis tests from her previous visit were expected to come back the following day.","\"If your pain stays under control and you have no bleeding, you can go home tonight,\" the doctor said. \"Return immediately if the pain worsens, you feel faint, or you notice any bleeding.\"","Serena nodded, but the moment he left, she turned to Alpha Sebastian.","\"Could we stay until the results come back? I don’t want to drive all the way here again tomorrow.\"","Alpha Sebastian glanced at the clock. \"You’re sure?\"","\"I’m exhausted, and my parents are already overwhelmed.\" She lowered her eyes. \"It would be easier to stay here.\"","He did not argue.","A nurse arranged overnight observation, and Serena settled back against the pillows.","She was about to say something else when her phone buzzed.","The screen showed a call from the Winthrop family.","Serena answered cautiously.","Her aunt’s voice exploded through the speaker.","\"Serena, do you think our house is your personal dumping ground? Stop sending your problems to our doorstep. Your grandfather is sick from all the stress you’ve caused him. And those court papers are going to your house. I’m having the driver take them there tonight.\"","The call ended before Serena could respond.","The color drained from her face.","Alpha Sebastian looked over. \"What happened?\"","She gripped the phone with both hands.","\"Eira filed the lawsuit,\" she whispered. \"She actually took me to court.\"","Alpha Sebastian did not look surprised.","\"I know.\"","Serena stared at him. Even her carefully applied makeup could not hide how pale she had become.","\"You knew? Then why didn’t you tell me?\"","\"What would you have done?\" Alpha Sebastian’s voice was flat. \"You can’t reach Eira, and neither can I. She made it clear from the beginning that she was prepared to sue.\"","\"But I was gathering the money.\"","\"The demand letter was a warning, not a settlement.\" Alpha Sebastian looked toward the dark window. \"It stated what she was demanding. It was not a court judgment.\"","Serena swallowed. \"What happens now?\"","\"You’ll be formally served with the complaint. After that, you’ll have a limited time to respond. If you ignore it, Eira can ask the court for a default judgment.\"","Serena stared at him. \"And if she wins?\"","\"Then she can try to enforce the judgment.\" His expression remained cold. \"She could seek a levy against your bank accounts, place liens on property in your name, and request a judgment debtor examination to find out what assets you have. Wage garnishment may also be possible if you have eligible income.\"","The words settled over the room like a blade.","Serena had already sold or listed almost everything she owned. Her apartment, her car, her jewelry, and even the investments her family had placed in her name would not come close to the amount Eira was demanding.","\"One hundred eighteen million dollars,\" she whispered. \"That’s what she wants?\"","\"That was the amount listed in the demand letter, including the money she says you took, damages, interest, and other costs.\" Alpha Sebastian glanced at her. \"It is not a final judgment yet, but you need a California attorney immediately.\"","Serena’s breathing turned shallow.","\"Can they stop me from leaving the country?\"","\"Not simply because Eira filed a lawsuit,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"But don’t move money, hide assets, transfer property, or lie in a sworn statement. If you ignore a court order or refuse to cooperate with the collection process, you could create a contempt issue and make everything worse.\""]},{"number":245,"title":"Chapter 245 No One Left to Call","paragraphs":["Serena’s heart sank.","She reached for Alpha Sebastian’s hand and lowered her voice into the soft, pleading tone that had always worked on him.","\"Sebastian, please. Can’t you talk to Eira? Ask her to drop the lawsuit?\"","Alpha Sebastian looked down at her. Her mascara had smudged beneath her eyes, and tears streaked her cheeks. She looked nothing like the polished, ambitious woman he had once believed she was.","The change unsettled him.","Serena noticed the distance in his eyes. He was looking at her as if she were a stranger who had wandered into his hospital room.","A sharp pain twisted through her chest, but she forced a brittle smile.","\"Do I have something on my face?\"","\"No.\" He looked away. \"It’s nothing. I can’t reach Eira, and I can’t make her drop the case.\"","\"Then what am I supposed to do?\"","\"Deal with it.\"","His jaw tightened.","Serena studied him.","Something about Alpha Sebastian had changed. He no longer looked guilty or angry. He looked empty, as if one blow too many had finally drained him of every reaction.","But Serena had no time to worry about him.","If Alpha Sebastian could not reach Eira, she would find someone who could.","Professor Davies.","\"I need some air,\" she muttered.","Before Alpha Sebastian could respond, she slipped out of the room and walked to the far end of the corridor. After checking that no one was nearby, she called Professor Davies.","He answered on the third attempt.","\"Professor Davies,\" Serena said, adding warmth to her voice. \"I was hoping you could arrange a meeting between Eira and me.\"","There was a pause.","\"Eira is traveling.\"","\"I mean when she gets back, of course.\" Serena smiled as if he could see her. \"I would really appreciate your help. My grandfather still has considerable influence at the Silix Institute. I could put in a good word for you. Surely you could do me this small favor.\"","His tone turned cold.","\"Serena, stop.\"","Her smile disappeared.","\"If you keep trying to manipulate people, you will drag Dr. Victor into this mess with you. I am not taking you anywhere near Eira. Let this go.\"","\"Professor Davies...\"","\"Your grandfather should have taught you better.\"","The line went dead.","Serena stared at the phone. Even her grandfather’s name had lost its power.","She was still searching for another name to use when she saw her parents coming down the hallway.","Robert looked grim. A sealed envelope hung from his hand.","Serena’s stomach tightened.","The demand letter had gone to her grandfather. Now the court papers had reached her parents.","\"Dad. Mom.\"","Robert held out the envelope.","Serena had no strength left to pretend. \"Open it.\"","They all knew what it was. Unlike a threatening letter, a court notice did not need dramatic language. It simply stated what would happen next.","Robert tore open the envelope.","Serena immediately looked at the date.","Her eyes widened.","\"The hearing is in four days.\"","Jennifer stepped closer. \"What kind of hearing?\"","Serena scanned the page again. \"It says eight-thirty in the morning. An emergency hearing on Eira’s request to preserve assets and prevent them from being transferred.\"","Robert’s expression changed.","This was not the trial. The judge would not decide the entire one-hundred-eighteen-million-dollar claim in four days. But if Eira won the emergency motion, Serena could face restrictions on her accounts and property while the lawsuit continued.","\"How did this happen so fast?\" Serena whispered.","Robert looked at the filing date. \"Because this is an emergency motion. The court can schedule a short hearing quickly if the plaintiff claims there is a risk that assets will be hidden or moved.\"","Serena’s fingers began to shake.","They had expected weeks to find a lawyer, sell property, and negotiate.","Now they had four days to respond.","The nightmare had not become impossible.","It had become immediate.","\"Dad, Mom, I need a lawyer,\" Serena said, her voice trembling. \"The best one we can get. Someone who handles high-stakes civil litigation and major financial disputes.\"","\"Your father and I will start calling firms now,\" Jennifer said.","Then a thought struck Serena.","\"Wait. There may be a way to fight this.\"","\"Sebastian and I signed an investment agreement. It said I wasn’t personally responsible for repaying the money if the project failed. The car and the condo were loans from him, but we agreed on how those payments would be described. And the jewelry was given to me as personal gifts. Those were gifts, not company assets.\"","A small spark of hope appeared in Jennifer’s eyes.","\"Why didn’t you tell us this earlier?\"","\"I forgot.\" Serena’s breathing eased, though her hands were still cold. \"There’s been too much happening. I didn’t realize those documents might matter.\"","Robert shook his head.","\"They might help us challenge some of Eira’s claims, but don’t assume they solve everything. Her attorney may argue that the agreements were false, that the gifts were disguised transfers, or that the money was obtained through fraud.\"","Serena’s brief relief faded.","\"Then we need someone who can explain all of it to the judge.\"","\"Exactly,\" Robert said. \"And we have four days.\"","The three of them agreed to begin the search immediately.","Serena placed the court papers back in the envelope.","\"You two should go home,\" she said. \"Sebastian is staying until my remaining test results come back tomorrow. I want the doctor to explain everything before I leave.\"","Jennifer’s expression softened with concern.","\"Were today’s results normal?\"","Serena nodded quickly. \"The ultrasound was fine. The doctor said there was no immediate emergency.\"","Robert glanced at the medical chart near the bed.","\"What are they waiting for tomorrow?\"","\"The prenatal infection screening,\" Serena replied smoothly. \"The HIV, hepatitis, and syphilis tests were sent to an outside lab. The rest of the results are already in.\"","Jennifer still looked worried.","\"You’ve been having stomach pain for days.\"","\"It’s stress.\" Serena forced a smile. \"I’m fine, Mom. The baby will be fine too.\"","Jennifer did not look convinced.","\"If you want me to feel better, go find us a lawyer,\" Serena said. \"We’re running out of time.\"","After a moment, Jennifer nodded.","\"Call us as soon as the results come in. I want to know exactly what the doctor says.\"","\"I will.\"","Robert picked up his coat. Before leaving, he looked at Serena for a long moment.","\"Do not move any money or sign anything without showing it to the attorney first.\"","Serena nodded, but her eyes shifted toward the sealed envelope."]}]);
